1
00:00:00,030 --> 00:00:07,900
Listen.

2
00:00:08,520 --> 00:00:09,040
Practice.

3
00:00:09,560 --> 00:00:09,900
Speak.

4
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:12,240
Practice makes you perfect.

5
00:00:14,020 --> 00:00:18,170
Hello, everyone, and welcome back to our English conversation practice session.

6
00:00:18,530 --> 00:00:18,970
I'm Ethan.

7
00:00:19,390 --> 00:00:19,970
And I'm Mia.

8
00:00:20,350 --> 00:00:22,910
We're so happy you're here learning English with us today.

9
00:00:23,270 --> 00:00:28,640
If you want to improve your spoken English for work and professional situations, you're in the right place.

10
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:29,260
That's right.

11
00:00:29,660 --> 00:00:33,390
Today's topic is business meeting conversations in 60 minutes.

12
00:00:33,930 --> 00:00:39,800
We're going to practice realistic office conversations that happen before, during, and after business meetings.

13
00:00:40,220 --> 00:00:47,790
You'll hear useful phrases for presenting ideas, discussing problems, asking questions, sharing opinions, and working with a team.

14
00:00:48,330 --> 00:00:53,920
And just like always, we'll use clear and natural English that sounds professional but easy to understand.

15
00:00:54,360 --> 00:00:57,340
All right, Isen, are you ready to start today's meeting practice?

16
00:00:57,540 --> 00:00:58,180
Absolutely.

17
00:00:58,340 --> 00:00:58,860
Let's begin.

18
00:00:59,280 --> 00:01:00,090
Good morning, Ethan.

19
00:01:00,330 --> 00:01:02,030
You're here earlier than usual today.

20
00:01:02,430 --> 00:01:02,990
Morning, Mia.

21
00:01:03,310 --> 00:01:06,050
Yeah, I wanted to prepare before the strategy meeting starts.

22
00:01:06,590 --> 00:01:07,060
Same here.

23
00:01:07,280 --> 00:01:09,060
Today's meeting sounds pretty important.

24
00:01:09,380 --> 00:01:09,900
Definitely.

25
00:01:10,360 --> 00:01:12,480
Management wants updates from every department.

26
00:01:12,890 --> 00:01:14,470
I heard the CEO will join too.

27
00:01:14,950 --> 00:01:15,230
Really?

28
00:01:15,450 --> 00:01:16,810
Then I'm even more nervous now.

29
00:01:18,050 --> 00:01:18,570
Don't worry.

30
00:01:18,670 --> 00:01:19,590
You're always prepared.

31
00:01:20,060 --> 00:01:20,740
I try to be.

32
00:01:21,160 --> 00:01:23,480
I reviewed my notes twice already this morning.

33
00:01:23,680 --> 00:01:24,420
That's a good habit.

34
00:01:24,780 --> 00:01:26,760
Preparation makes meetings less stressful.

35
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:27,700
Exactly.

36
00:01:28,190 --> 00:01:29,770
Did you finish your presentation slides?

37
00:01:30,270 --> 00:01:30,710
Almost.

38
00:01:30,970 --> 00:01:33,330
I'm still changing a few things on the final slide.

39
00:01:33,810 --> 00:01:34,430
What's wrong with it?

40
00:01:34,770 --> 00:01:36,500
I think there's too much information.

41
00:01:37,060 --> 00:01:38,720
That happens a lot with presentations.

42
00:01:39,260 --> 00:01:39,600
Yeah.

43
00:01:39,820 --> 00:01:42,120
I want it to look professional, but still simple.

44
00:01:42,620 --> 00:01:44,920
Maybe use fewer words and add more visuals.

45
00:01:45,340 --> 00:01:45,860
Good idea.

46
00:01:46,250 --> 00:01:48,170
Charts usually explain things faster.

47
00:01:48,650 --> 00:01:49,150
Exactly.

48
00:01:49,470 --> 00:01:51,930
Especially during meetings where time is limited.

49
00:01:52,050 --> 00:01:56,210
Speaking of time, this meeting is scheduled for exactly 60 minutes.

50
00:01:56,770 --> 00:01:59,860
That means everyone needs to keep their updates short and clear.

51
00:02:00,260 --> 00:02:02,560
Which is honestly harder than it sounds.

52
00:02:03,140 --> 00:02:03,790
Very true.

53
00:02:04,250 --> 00:02:07,630
Some people turn 5-minute updates into 20-minute speeches.

54
00:02:09,090 --> 00:02:10,520
We all know who you're talking about.

55
00:02:11,080 --> 00:02:12,160
I'm not naming names.

56
00:02:12,680 --> 00:02:13,020
All right.

57
00:02:13,100 --> 00:02:14,340
Should we go to the conference room?

58
00:02:14,780 --> 00:02:15,020
Sure.

59
00:02:15,180 --> 00:02:16,450
Let's grab coffee first, though.

60
00:02:16,770 --> 00:02:18,110
I'll need extra energy today.

61
00:02:18,590 --> 00:02:19,270
Same here.

62
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:20,400
Good morning, everyone.

63
00:02:20,640 --> 00:02:23,190
Thanks for joining today's business meeting conversation.

64
00:02:23,530 --> 00:02:24,010
Good morning.

65
00:02:24,470 --> 00:02:25,150
Morning, everyone.

66
00:02:25,550 --> 00:02:28,340
Since we only have 60 minutes, let's begin right away.

67
00:02:28,740 --> 00:02:29,240
Good idea.

68
00:02:29,680 --> 00:02:32,440
First, we'll review project progress from each department.

69
00:02:32,780 --> 00:02:35,000
Then we'll discuss next month's goals.

70
00:02:35,020 --> 00:02:35,490
Sounds good.

71
00:02:35,940 --> 00:02:38,030
Ethan, would you like to start with the marketing update?

72
00:02:38,490 --> 00:02:38,890
Of course.

73
00:02:39,390 --> 00:02:42,660
Over the past month, our online engagement increased by 12%.

74
00:02:43,010 --> 00:02:44,480
That's excellent news.

75
00:02:44,940 --> 00:02:46,540
What contributed to the increase?

76
00:02:46,690 --> 00:02:50,790
mainly short-form video campaigns and stronger social media interaction.

77
00:02:51,190 --> 00:02:51,650
Interesting.

78
00:02:51,950 --> 00:02:53,510
Which platform performed best?

79
00:02:54,040 --> 00:02:56,540
Instagram generated the highest audience engagement.

80
00:02:56,880 --> 00:02:57,540
That makes sense.

81
00:02:57,780 --> 00:03:00,220
Video content is extremely popular right now.

82
00:03:00,660 --> 00:03:01,180
Exactly.

83
00:03:01,540 --> 00:03:05,390
We also noticed customers responding positively to behind-the-scenes content.

84
00:03:05,750 --> 00:03:06,950
That's valuable information.

85
00:03:07,450 --> 00:03:10,410
However, email campaign performance dropped slightly.

86
00:03:10,770 --> 00:03:11,440
Do we know why?

87
00:03:11,470 --> 00:03:14,520
We believe the messages were too long and formal.

88
00:03:14,630 --> 00:03:15,210
I agree.

89
00:03:15,270 --> 00:03:19,080
Usually, customers prefer shorter and more personal communication.

90
00:03:19,540 --> 00:03:21,360
That's what our research suggests as well.

91
00:03:21,820 --> 00:03:23,340
So, what changes are you planning?

92
00:03:23,720 --> 00:03:28,130
We'd like to redesign the email format and focus more on personalized messaging.

93
00:03:28,610 --> 00:03:29,730
Sounds like a smart approach.

94
00:03:30,190 --> 00:03:30,510
Thank you.

95
00:03:30,950 --> 00:03:33,500
All right, let's move on to the sales department update.

96
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:34,640
Good morning, everyone.

97
00:03:35,140 --> 00:03:37,960
Overall sales increased by 8% this quarter.

98
00:03:38,340 --> 00:03:39,060
Great progress.

99
00:03:39,540 --> 00:03:39,880
Thank you.

100
00:03:40,380 --> 00:03:43,630
However, we faced delays in two major client projects.

101
00:03:43,830 --> 00:03:45,010
What caused the delays?

102
00:03:45,570 --> 00:03:48,410
Mostly supply chain issues and late product deliveries.

103
00:03:48,890 --> 00:03:50,260
Are those issues resolved now?

104
00:03:50,840 --> 00:03:54,100
Mostly, yes, but we're still monitoring the situation carefully.

105
00:03:54,440 --> 00:03:54,680
Good.

106
00:03:54,920 --> 00:03:57,870
Keeping clients informed is very important during delays.

107
00:03:58,430 --> 00:03:59,010
Absolutely.

108
00:03:59,430 --> 00:04:01,610
Communication helped us avoid bigger problems.

109
00:04:02,070 --> 00:04:03,940
Did any clients react negatively?

110
00:04:03,970 --> 00:04:08,940
A few were frustrated at first, but they appreciated our honesty and regular updates.

111
00:04:09,420 --> 00:04:12,690
Transparency is always important in business relationships.

112
00:04:12,920 --> 00:04:14,060
I completely agree.

113
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:14,900
Excellent.

114
00:04:15,040 --> 00:04:15,900
Thank you for the update.

115
00:04:16,310 --> 00:04:17,930
Excuse me, may I add something?

116
00:04:18,330 --> 00:04:18,710
Of course.

117
00:04:18,870 --> 00:04:19,290
Go ahead.

118
00:04:19,710 --> 00:04:23,210
I think departments should communicate more frequently during large projects.

119
00:04:23,690 --> 00:04:24,820
What do you mean exactly?

120
00:04:25,320 --> 00:04:30,120
Sometimes marketing, sales, and operations work separately without sharing enough information.

121
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:32,050
That's actually a very good point.

122
00:04:32,510 --> 00:04:35,790
Better communication could help us avoid delays and misunderstandings.

123
00:04:36,230 --> 00:04:37,070
I agree completely.

124
00:04:37,560 --> 00:04:40,400
Maybe we could organize shorter weekly communication meetings.

125
00:04:40,840 --> 00:04:42,300
That sounds like a great idea.

126
00:04:42,350 --> 00:04:43,570
It wouldn't need to be long.

127
00:04:43,610 --> 00:04:45,430
Even 15 minutes could help.

128
00:04:45,910 --> 00:04:47,380
That sounds practical and efficient.

129
00:04:47,800 --> 00:04:48,860
Great suggestion, Ethan.

130
00:04:49,220 --> 00:04:49,540
Thanks.

131
00:04:50,080 --> 00:04:50,760
All right, everyone.

132
00:04:51,140 --> 00:04:52,820
Let's discuss next month's goals.

133
00:04:53,340 --> 00:04:57,520
The company wants to improve customer satisfaction and internal communication.

134
00:04:58,000 --> 00:04:59,690
Those are both important priorities.

135
00:05:00,210 --> 00:05:00,710
Exactly.

136
00:05:01,090 --> 00:05:05,070
We also want to reduce project delays by improving workflow efficiency.

137
00:05:05,530 --> 00:05:08,480
That will require stronger teamwork across departments.

138
00:05:08,590 --> 00:05:09,270
Absolutely.

139
00:05:09,310 --> 00:05:11,780
I have a question about the new workflow system.

140
00:05:12,220 --> 00:05:12,460
Sure.

141
00:05:12,820 --> 00:05:15,480
Will employees receive training before implementation?

142
00:05:15,920 --> 00:05:16,180
Yes.

143
00:05:16,440 --> 00:05:18,470
Training sessions will begin next Monday.

144
00:05:18,810 --> 00:05:19,050
Good.

145
00:05:19,330 --> 00:05:20,730
That should make the transition easier.

146
00:05:21,170 --> 00:05:23,800
We want everyone to feel comfortable using the new system.

147
00:05:24,260 --> 00:05:24,980
That's important.

148
00:05:25,420 --> 00:05:27,300
Sudden changes can create confusion.

149
00:05:27,740 --> 00:05:28,240
Exactly.

150
00:05:28,700 --> 00:05:31,510
By the way, do we know when the software upgrade will happen?

151
00:05:31,620 --> 00:05:34,670
IT plans to complete installation by the end of the month.

152
00:05:35,130 --> 00:05:35,530
Perfect.

153
00:05:35,870 --> 00:05:38,840
We'll also provide technical support during the first few weeks.

154
00:05:39,360 --> 00:05:43,750
That's reassuring, especially for employees who aren't very comfortable with technology yet.

155
00:05:44,990 --> 00:05:46,290
I know a few people like that.

156
00:05:46,850 --> 00:05:48,200
I think every office has them.

157
00:05:48,560 --> 00:05:48,860
True.

158
00:05:49,300 --> 00:05:51,780
All right, everyone, we still have 20 minutes left.

159
00:05:51,820 --> 00:05:54,210
Let's open the floor for questions and ideas.

160
00:05:54,390 --> 00:05:57,150
I'd like to suggest something regarding team productivity.

161
00:05:57,500 --> 00:05:57,920
Go ahead.

162
00:05:58,320 --> 00:06:01,480
I think too many long meetings reduce efficiency sometimes.

163
00:06:01,920 --> 00:06:02,640
Interesting point.

164
00:06:03,190 --> 00:06:07,030
Some meetings could probably be shorter or handled through email updates instead.

165
00:06:07,430 --> 00:06:08,780
Honestly, I agree with that.

166
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:12,660
People lose focus when meetings last too long without clear goals.

167
00:06:13,220 --> 00:06:13,810
Very true.

168
00:06:14,270 --> 00:06:17,290
Maybe we should create stricter meeting schedules and agendas.

169
00:06:17,420 --> 00:06:19,190
That would help everyone stay organized.

170
00:06:19,650 --> 00:06:20,170
Exactly.

171
00:06:20,590 --> 00:06:24,830
I think shorter meetings with clear action points would improve productivity significantly.

172
00:06:25,250 --> 00:06:25,870
Great idea.

173
00:06:26,230 --> 00:06:29,220
We should also encourage employees to prepare before meetings.

174
00:06:29,720 --> 00:06:31,440
Preparation saves a lot of time.

175
00:06:31,860 --> 00:06:32,380
Definitely.

176
00:06:32,920 --> 00:06:34,040
I have another suggestion.

177
00:06:34,500 --> 00:06:34,760
Sure.

178
00:06:35,240 --> 00:06:37,870
Maybe we could organize monthly team-building activities.

179
00:06:38,330 --> 00:06:39,030
That sounds fun.

180
00:06:39,530 --> 00:06:43,610
Better relationships between coworkers often improve communication and teamwork.

181
00:06:44,030 --> 00:06:44,890
I completely agree.

182
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:47,280
What kind of activities are you thinking about?

183
00:06:47,440 --> 00:06:51,430
Maybe group lunches, outdoor events, or problem-solving games.

184
00:06:51,950 --> 00:06:53,310
Escape rooms could be interesting.

185
00:06:53,850 --> 00:06:55,580
Oh, that would actually be really fun.

186
00:06:56,020 --> 00:06:58,440
Plus, they require teamwork and communication skills.

187
00:06:58,940 --> 00:06:59,540
Exactly.

188
00:07:00,020 --> 00:07:00,750
All right, everyone.

189
00:07:00,960 --> 00:07:04,170
Before we finish, let's review today's action points.

190
00:07:04,190 --> 00:07:07,800
First, the marketing team will redesign the email campaign strategy.

191
00:07:08,300 --> 00:07:11,600
Second, departments will begin shorter weekly communication meetings.

192
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:15,850
Third, employee training for the new workflow system starts Monday.

193
00:07:15,950 --> 00:07:20,090
And finally, management will discuss ideas for future team building activities.

194
00:07:20,550 --> 00:07:21,290
Perfect summary.

195
00:07:21,630 --> 00:07:24,340
Does anyone have final questions before we end today's meeting?

196
00:07:24,740 --> 00:07:25,360
Nothing from me.

197
00:07:25,380 --> 00:07:26,420
I'm good too.

198
00:07:26,460 --> 00:07:27,340
All right then.

199
00:07:27,600 --> 00:07:30,240
Thank you everyone for your time and participation today.

200
00:07:30,660 --> 00:07:31,020
Thank you.

201
00:07:31,060 --> 00:07:32,050
Thanks everyone.

202
00:07:32,440 --> 00:07:33,630
Great meeting today, Mia.

203
00:07:33,970 --> 00:07:34,290
Thanks.

204
00:07:34,570 --> 00:07:35,990
I think everything went smoothly.

205
00:07:36,450 --> 00:07:38,570
And we actually finished within 60 minutes.

206
00:07:39,030 --> 00:07:40,950
That might be the most impressive part.

207
00:07:41,800 --> 00:07:42,320
Very true.

208
00:07:42,740 --> 00:07:45,800
Honestly, shorter meetings feel much more productive.

209
00:07:45,930 --> 00:07:46,980
I agree completely.

210
00:07:47,380 --> 00:07:49,740
People stay focused when discussions are organized.

211
00:07:50,160 --> 00:07:50,700
Exactly.

212
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:53,620
I also liked hearing ideas from different departments.

213
00:07:54,120 --> 00:07:54,590
Same here.

214
00:07:54,970 --> 00:07:57,510
Cross-department communication is really important.

215
00:07:57,870 --> 00:07:58,370
Definitely.

216
00:07:58,890 --> 00:08:01,480
Sometimes teams become too isolated from each other.

217
00:08:01,900 --> 00:08:03,780
And that creates misunderstandings later.

218
00:08:03,820 --> 00:08:04,860
Exactly.

219
00:08:05,480 --> 00:08:08,530
By the way, your suggestion about shorter meetings was excellent.

220
00:08:08,910 --> 00:08:09,550
Thanks.

221
00:08:09,570 --> 00:08:11,590
I've honestly been thinking about it for months.

222
00:08:12,750 --> 00:08:13,490
I could tell.

223
00:08:13,540 --> 00:08:14,740
What about your presentation?

224
00:08:14,780 --> 00:08:16,440
You looked very confident today.

225
00:08:16,850 --> 00:08:17,080
Really?

226
00:08:17,450 --> 00:08:18,710
I was nervous before speaking.

227
00:08:19,130 --> 00:08:20,470
Honestly, nobody could tell.

228
00:08:20,950 --> 00:08:21,610
That's good to hear.

229
00:08:21,670 --> 00:08:24,380
Your explanations were very clear and professional.

230
00:08:24,760 --> 00:08:25,100
Thanks.

231
00:08:25,320 --> 00:08:26,660
I practiced a lot last night.

232
00:08:27,080 --> 00:08:28,380
Practice definitely helps.

233
00:08:28,860 --> 00:08:29,560
It really does.

234
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:31,290
Hey, are you free for lunch now?

235
00:08:31,730 --> 00:08:32,250
Absolutely.

236
00:08:32,290 --> 00:08:33,850
I'm starving after that meeting.

237
00:08:34,350 --> 00:08:34,630
Same.

238
00:08:35,070 --> 00:08:36,770
My brain needs food immediately.

239
00:08:37,980 --> 00:08:39,100
Let's invite the others, too.

240
00:08:39,580 --> 00:08:40,060
Good idea.

241
00:08:40,560 --> 00:08:42,060
Team lunches are always fun.

242
00:08:42,180 --> 00:08:45,280
Plus, people communicate more naturally outside formal meetings.

243
00:08:45,800 --> 00:08:46,300
That's true.

244
00:08:46,840 --> 00:08:49,830
Some of the best ideas happen during casual conversations.

245
00:08:50,310 --> 00:08:50,810
Exactly.

246
00:08:51,290 --> 00:08:52,430
So, where should we go today?

247
00:08:52,870 --> 00:08:55,640
There's a new restaurant near the office everyone's talking about.

248
00:08:56,060 --> 00:08:56,460
Perfect.

249
00:08:56,640 --> 00:08:57,160
Let's try it.

250
00:08:57,580 --> 00:08:58,060
Sounds good.

251
00:08:58,480 --> 00:09:04,170
Well, everyone, we hope today's conversation helped you learn useful English for business meetings and office communication.

252
00:09:04,530 --> 00:09:08,220
These are practical phrases and expressions you can use at work every day.

253
00:09:08,280 --> 00:09:12,490
Try practicing them with friends, co-workers, or even by yourself out loud.

254
00:09:12,910 --> 00:09:16,410
The more you practice, the more confident and natural your English will become.

255
00:09:16,830 --> 00:09:18,030
Thanks for learning with us today.

256
00:09:18,500 --> 00:09:21,900
And we'll see you again next time with more Real English Conversations.

257
00:09:22,380 --> 00:09:23,160
Take care, everyone.

258
00:09:23,480 --> 00:09:24,040
Bye, everyone.

259
00:09:26,760 --> 00:09:27,520
Hello, everyone.

260
00:09:27,730 --> 00:09:30,010
Welcome back to our English Learning Podcast.

261
00:09:30,430 --> 00:09:32,030
We're so happy you joined us today.

262
00:09:32,530 --> 00:09:33,050
I'm Ryan.

263
00:09:33,370 --> 00:09:34,270
And I'm Chloe.

264
00:09:34,420 --> 00:09:38,870
Today we have another practical English lesson for office workers and business professionals.

265
00:09:39,350 --> 00:09:39,790
That's right.

266
00:09:40,190 --> 00:09:44,160
Today's topic is business meeting conversations in 60 minutes.

267
00:09:44,760 --> 00:09:47,440
In many companies, meetings are scheduled for one hour.

268
00:09:47,940 --> 00:09:54,290
During that time, people discuss projects, solve problems, give updates, make decisions, and share ideas.

269
00:09:54,830 --> 00:10:00,380
So today we'll practice realistic business conversations that happen during a typical one-hour office meeting.

270
00:10:00,650 --> 00:10:09,440
You'll learn useful English phrases for starting meetings, presenting ideas, discussing deadlines, handling disagreements, and ending meetings professionally.

271
00:10:09,920 --> 00:10:10,560
And don't worry.

272
00:10:10,900 --> 00:10:14,260
We'll use clear and natural English so you can follow along easily.

273
00:10:14,300 --> 00:10:15,160
All right.

274
00:10:15,630 --> 00:10:16,090
Let's begin.

275
00:10:16,530 --> 00:10:17,250
Good morning, Chloe.

276
00:10:17,590 --> 00:10:18,310
Good morning, Ryan.

277
00:10:18,550 --> 00:10:19,530
You're here early today.

278
00:10:20,010 --> 00:10:22,630
I wanted to prepare the conference room before the team arrived.

279
00:10:23,020 --> 00:10:23,760
That's responsible.

280
00:10:24,180 --> 00:10:25,400
Today's meeting is important.

281
00:10:25,760 --> 00:10:26,300
Definitely.

282
00:10:26,700 --> 00:10:29,400
The management team wants updates on every department.

283
00:10:29,600 --> 00:10:31,500
I heard the CEO might join the meeting too.

284
00:10:31,880 --> 00:10:32,190
Really?

285
00:10:32,230 --> 00:10:32,890
Yes.

286
00:10:33,290 --> 00:10:35,390
Then we should make sure everything is organized.

287
00:10:35,810 --> 00:10:36,110
Agreed.

288
00:10:36,530 --> 00:10:38,150
Did you print the presentation handouts?

289
00:10:38,590 --> 00:10:40,880
Yes, I printed enough copies for everyone.

290
00:10:41,200 --> 00:10:41,600
Perfect.

291
00:10:42,080 --> 00:10:44,280
I also prepared coffee and water for the meeting.

292
00:10:44,740 --> 00:10:45,480
Excellent planning.

293
00:10:45,820 --> 00:10:46,100
Thanks.

294
00:10:46,620 --> 00:10:48,280
By the way, how was your commute this morning?

295
00:10:48,700 --> 00:10:49,660
Surprisingly smooth.

296
00:10:50,040 --> 00:10:50,610
Lucky you.

297
00:10:50,640 --> 00:10:52,110
Traffic was bad for you?

298
00:10:52,530 --> 00:10:53,030
Terrible.

299
00:10:53,430 --> 00:10:53,970
What happened?

300
00:10:54,390 --> 00:10:55,990
There was construction near the highway.

301
00:10:56,410 --> 00:10:57,150
That explains it.

302
00:10:57,530 --> 00:10:59,370
I spent almost an hour in traffic.

303
00:10:59,640 --> 00:11:00,800
That sounds exhausting.

304
00:11:01,200 --> 00:11:02,280
At least I made it on time.

305
00:11:02,720 --> 00:11:03,400
That's what matters.

306
00:11:03,910 --> 00:11:04,270
All right.

307
00:11:04,390 --> 00:11:05,630
Looks like everyone is arriving.

308
00:11:06,050 --> 00:11:06,750
Let's get started.

309
00:11:07,170 --> 00:11:08,010
Good morning, everyone.

310
00:11:08,250 --> 00:11:10,110
Thank you for joining today's business meeting.

311
00:11:10,490 --> 00:11:13,640
We have several important topics to discuss, so let's begin.

312
00:11:14,100 --> 00:11:16,260
First, let's review last month's performance.

313
00:11:16,840 --> 00:11:19,220
Overall, our company achieved strong results.

314
00:11:19,760 --> 00:11:22,670
Sales increased by 22% compared to last quarter.

315
00:11:23,070 --> 00:11:24,570
That's excellent progress.

316
00:11:24,680 --> 00:11:27,290
Customer engagement also improved significantly.

317
00:11:27,710 --> 00:11:28,190
Great news.

318
00:11:28,670 --> 00:11:30,830
However, we still face a few challenges.

319
00:11:31,370 --> 00:11:31,790
Such as?

320
00:11:32,250 --> 00:11:35,340
Project delays and communication issues between departments.

321
00:11:35,880 --> 00:11:36,880
I've noticed that too.

322
00:11:37,360 --> 00:11:39,080
Especially during large projects.

323
00:11:39,600 --> 00:11:41,450
Better coordination would definitely help.

324
00:11:41,880 --> 00:11:42,270
Agreed.

325
00:11:42,690 --> 00:11:45,630
All right, let's hear updates from the marketing department first.

326
00:11:46,090 --> 00:11:46,450
Thank you.

327
00:11:46,870 --> 00:11:49,220
Our latest campaign performed better than expected.

328
00:11:49,600 --> 00:11:50,260
That's wonderful.

329
00:11:50,720 --> 00:11:52,960
Social media engagement increased by 40%.

330
00:11:53,820 --> 00:11:54,520
Impressive.

331
00:11:54,670 --> 00:11:58,010
Website traffic also grew rapidly after the campaign launch.

332
00:11:58,430 --> 00:12:00,180
What contributed most to the success?

333
00:12:00,760 --> 00:12:03,300
Video advertisements and influencer partnerships.

334
00:12:03,840 --> 00:12:04,280
Interesting.

335
00:12:04,620 --> 00:12:07,560
Customers responded positively to authentic content.

336
00:12:08,020 --> 00:12:08,710
That makes sense.

337
00:12:09,170 --> 00:12:12,610
We also improved communication with customers through live chat support.

338
00:12:13,030 --> 00:12:13,770
Excellent idea.

339
00:12:14,210 --> 00:12:16,870
Faster responses improved customer satisfaction.

340
00:12:17,290 --> 00:12:19,220
Were there any difficulties during the campaign?

341
00:12:19,700 --> 00:12:20,040
Yes.

342
00:12:20,580 --> 00:12:21,640
What kind of difficulties?

343
00:12:22,100 --> 00:12:24,000
The team faced tight deadlines.

344
00:12:24,150 --> 00:12:25,770
That can create a lot of pressure.

345
00:12:26,110 --> 00:12:26,670
Definitely.

346
00:12:27,120 --> 00:12:28,200
How did the team handle it?

347
00:12:28,580 --> 00:12:31,260
We scheduled shorter daily meetings to track progress.

348
00:12:31,740 --> 00:12:32,300
Did that help?

349
00:12:32,760 --> 00:12:33,260
Very much.

350
00:12:33,740 --> 00:12:35,280
Communication became more efficient?

351
00:12:35,660 --> 00:12:36,120
Exactly.

352
00:12:36,570 --> 00:12:37,090
Great work.

353
00:12:37,450 --> 00:12:37,810
Thank you.

354
00:12:38,250 --> 00:12:40,070
Next, let's hear from the finance department.

355
00:12:40,530 --> 00:12:41,350
Good morning, everyone.

356
00:12:41,810 --> 00:12:44,510
Overall, the financial situation looks stable.

357
00:12:44,540 --> 00:12:45,180
That's good to hear.

358
00:12:45,620 --> 00:12:47,940
However, some departments exceeded their budgets.

359
00:12:48,420 --> 00:12:49,140
Which departments?

360
00:12:49,720 --> 00:12:51,280
Marketing and product development.

361
00:12:51,680 --> 00:12:52,280
By how much?

362
00:12:52,850 --> 00:12:54,110
Around 10%.

363
00:12:54,190 --> 00:12:55,210
That's not ideal.

364
00:12:55,690 --> 00:12:58,690
No, but the additional spending produced strong results.

365
00:12:59,120 --> 00:13:00,280
That's important.

366
00:13:00,300 --> 00:13:02,580
Sometimes strategic investment is necessary.

367
00:13:02,900 --> 00:13:03,280
I agree.

368
00:13:03,760 --> 00:13:06,560
Still, we should monitor expenses carefully next quarter.

369
00:13:06,950 --> 00:13:07,450
Definitely.

370
00:13:07,850 --> 00:13:10,390
We also need to reduce unnecessary travel costs.

371
00:13:10,890 --> 00:13:12,930
Maybe we can schedule more virtual meetings.

372
00:13:13,430 --> 00:13:14,130
Good suggestion.

373
00:13:14,510 --> 00:13:16,340
That would save both money and time.

374
00:13:16,780 --> 00:13:17,300
Exactly.

375
00:13:17,680 --> 00:13:20,460
All right, let's move on to project management updates.

376
00:13:20,980 --> 00:13:23,490
The Wilson project is currently behind schedule.

377
00:13:23,700 --> 00:13:24,660
What caused the delay?

378
00:13:25,090 --> 00:13:27,750
We encountered technical issues during system integration.

379
00:13:28,170 --> 00:13:29,410
How serious are the issues?

380
00:13:29,950 --> 00:13:31,410
More serious than we expected.

381
00:13:31,830 --> 00:13:32,770
Do we have a solution?

382
00:13:33,170 --> 00:13:35,000
The IT department is working on it now.

383
00:13:35,460 --> 00:13:36,340
How long will it take?

384
00:13:36,740 --> 00:13:38,300
Approximately two more weeks.

385
00:13:38,740 --> 00:13:39,800
Will the client be affected?

386
00:13:40,250 --> 00:13:40,880
Most likely.

387
00:13:41,310 --> 00:13:42,310
Have we informed them yet?

388
00:13:42,750 --> 00:13:43,510
Not officially.

389
00:13:43,950 --> 00:13:45,690
We should communicate with them immediately.

390
00:13:45,730 --> 00:13:46,610
I agree.

391
00:13:47,030 --> 00:13:48,550
Clients appreciate transparency.

392
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:49,520
Exactly.

393
00:13:49,920 --> 00:13:53,640
We should explain the situation clearly and provide a revised timeline.

394
00:13:53,770 --> 00:13:55,900
I'll prepare a detailed report this afternoon.

395
00:13:56,300 --> 00:13:56,720
Perfect.

396
00:13:57,160 --> 00:13:59,320
All right, everyone, let's take a short coffee break.

397
00:13:59,780 --> 00:14:00,160
Finally.

398
00:14:00,610 --> 00:14:01,890
I think everyone needed that.

399
00:14:02,270 --> 00:14:02,770
Definitely.

400
00:14:03,210 --> 00:14:05,270
So, how are things going in your department lately?

401
00:14:05,630 --> 00:14:06,840
Busy, but manageable.

402
00:14:07,220 --> 00:14:07,660
That's good.

403
00:14:08,020 --> 00:14:09,860
We recently hired two new employees.

404
00:14:10,300 --> 00:14:10,580
Really?

405
00:14:10,960 --> 00:14:11,220
Yes.

406
00:14:11,720 --> 00:14:12,540
How are they adjusting?

407
00:14:12,860 --> 00:14:13,300
Pretty well.

408
00:14:13,650 --> 00:14:14,130
That's great.

409
00:14:14,470 --> 00:14:16,450
They're still learning our software systems, though.

410
00:14:16,790 --> 00:14:17,490
That takes time.

411
00:14:17,910 --> 00:14:18,410
Exactly.

412
00:14:18,850 --> 00:14:20,780
Do you enjoy training new employees?

413
00:14:20,840 --> 00:14:21,680
Honestly, yes.

414
00:14:22,180 --> 00:14:22,460
Really?

415
00:14:22,900 --> 00:14:25,230
I like helping people feel comfortable in the workplace.

416
00:14:25,710 --> 00:14:26,390
That's important.

417
00:14:26,770 --> 00:14:28,670
Starting a new job can feel overwhelming.

418
00:14:29,170 --> 00:14:29,770
Very true.

419
00:14:30,090 --> 00:14:30,550
What about you?

420
00:14:30,570 --> 00:14:32,520
I enjoy mentoring people, too.

421
00:14:32,960 --> 00:14:34,380
Good leaders support their teams.

422
00:14:34,900 --> 00:14:35,460
Absolutely.

423
00:14:35,860 --> 00:14:38,380
By the way, congratulations on your recent promotion.

424
00:14:38,760 --> 00:14:39,120
Thank you.

425
00:14:39,470 --> 00:14:40,000
How does it feel?

426
00:14:40,430 --> 00:14:42,270
Exciting, but also challenging.

427
00:14:42,730 --> 00:14:43,770
More responsibilities?

428
00:14:44,290 --> 00:14:44,990
A lot more.

429
00:14:45,470 --> 00:14:46,390
I can imagine.

430
00:14:46,440 --> 00:14:48,740
Now I attend meetings almost all day.

431
00:14:48,800 --> 00:14:50,110
Welcome to management.

432
00:14:50,430 --> 00:14:53,290
Honestly, I miss having quiet work time sometimes.

433
00:14:53,690 --> 00:14:55,110
That happens to many managers.

434
00:14:55,610 --> 00:14:58,700
Still, I enjoy leading projects and helping the team succeed.

435
00:14:59,120 --> 00:15:00,060
That's a great attitude.

436
00:15:00,480 --> 00:15:01,980
All right, looks like the break is over.

437
00:15:02,360 --> 00:15:03,060
Time to continue.

438
00:15:03,420 --> 00:15:04,360
Welcome back, everyone.

439
00:15:04,800 --> 00:15:07,130
Let's continue with the next agenda item.

440
00:15:07,150 --> 00:15:09,970
We need to discuss employee workload and productivity.

441
00:15:10,430 --> 00:15:12,670
Several teams have been working overtime recently.

442
00:15:13,090 --> 00:15:14,580
Yes, I've noticed that.

443
00:15:14,690 --> 00:15:16,510
Employee stress levels are increasing.

444
00:15:16,870 --> 00:15:17,650
That's concerning.

445
00:15:18,110 --> 00:15:20,660
Burnout can affect both productivity and morale.

446
00:15:21,080 --> 00:15:22,060
I completely agree.

447
00:15:22,440 --> 00:15:23,660
Do you have any suggestions?

448
00:15:24,160 --> 00:15:27,180
We could redistribute tasks more evenly between teams.

449
00:15:27,660 --> 00:15:28,140
Good idea.

450
00:15:28,530 --> 00:15:31,030
We might also consider hiring temporary staff.

451
00:15:31,490 --> 00:15:33,590
That could reduce pressure during busy periods.

452
00:15:34,050 --> 00:15:34,550
Exactly.

453
00:15:34,970 --> 00:15:36,530
Another issue is communication.

454
00:15:36,960 --> 00:15:38,460
What kind of communication problems?

455
00:15:38,940 --> 00:15:41,420
Some employees feel uncomfortable asking for help.

456
00:15:41,820 --> 00:15:44,120
That happens often in stressful environments.

457
00:15:44,320 --> 00:15:46,550
Managers should encourage open communication.

458
00:15:47,030 --> 00:15:47,550
Definitely.

459
00:15:47,950 --> 00:15:49,450
Team members should feel supported.

460
00:15:49,870 --> 00:15:50,310
I agree.

461
00:15:50,690 --> 00:15:54,340
We could also organize wellness workshops or stress management sessions.

462
00:15:54,780 --> 00:15:55,880
That's an excellent idea.

463
00:15:56,260 --> 00:15:58,070
Mental health is important in the workplace.

464
00:15:58,610 --> 00:15:59,190
Absolutely.

465
00:15:59,590 --> 00:15:59,910
All right.

466
00:16:00,210 --> 00:16:02,240
Now let's discuss future company goals.

467
00:16:02,900 --> 00:16:05,520
One major goal is expanding into international markets.

468
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:06,580
Exciting.

469
00:16:06,770 --> 00:16:09,510
We're currently researching opportunities in Europe and Asia.

470
00:16:09,890 --> 00:16:11,530
That could create significant growth.

471
00:16:11,970 --> 00:16:12,470
Exactly.

472
00:16:12,910 --> 00:16:14,320
What challenges do you expect?

473
00:16:14,780 --> 00:16:16,940
Cultural differences and local competition.

474
00:16:17,300 --> 00:16:18,540
Those are important factors.

475
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:21,790
We'll need strong market research before making decisions.

476
00:16:22,290 --> 00:16:22,750
Definitely.

477
00:16:23,250 --> 00:16:25,790
Another goal is improving sustainability practices.

478
00:16:26,230 --> 00:16:29,140
Customers care more about environmental responsibility now.

479
00:16:29,620 --> 00:16:30,200
Very true.

480
00:16:30,600 --> 00:16:31,920
What changes are we considering?

481
00:16:32,360 --> 00:16:35,120
Reducing paper waste and improving energy efficiency.

482
00:16:35,490 --> 00:16:36,490
Good initiatives.

483
00:16:36,530 --> 00:16:39,140
We also want to work with more eco-friendly suppliers.

484
00:16:39,640 --> 00:16:41,560
That would strengthen the company's reputation.

485
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:42,520
Exactly.

486
00:16:42,900 --> 00:16:46,700
All right, before we finish, does anyone have additional comments or questions?

487
00:16:47,200 --> 00:16:49,630
I have one question regarding remote work policies.

488
00:16:50,050 --> 00:16:50,450
Go ahead.

489
00:16:50,870 --> 00:16:53,330
Will employees continue working from home part-time?

490
00:16:53,730 --> 00:16:54,570
At the moment, yes.

491
00:16:55,030 --> 00:16:55,690
That's good news.

492
00:16:56,070 --> 00:16:59,180
Management believes flexible work schedules improve productivity.

493
00:16:59,620 --> 00:17:00,540
I agree completely.

494
00:17:00,880 --> 00:17:03,800
However, teams still need regular in-person meetings.

495
00:17:04,300 --> 00:17:04,900
Of course.

496
00:17:05,100 --> 00:17:08,090
Face-to-face communication remains important for collaboration.

497
00:17:08,590 --> 00:17:09,090
Definitely.

498
00:17:09,470 --> 00:17:10,280
Any other questions?

499
00:17:10,820 --> 00:17:11,400
Nothing from me.

500
00:17:11,780 --> 00:17:12,100
All right.

501
00:17:12,520 --> 00:17:13,900
Then let's wrap up today's meeting.

502
00:17:14,250 --> 00:17:16,830
Thank you everyone for your hard work and participation.

503
00:17:17,190 --> 00:17:19,700
Please send your updated reports by Friday afternoon.

504
00:17:20,180 --> 00:17:22,490
And don't forget next week's strategy meeting.

505
00:17:22,600 --> 00:17:23,880
Have a productive day, everyone.

506
00:17:24,200 --> 00:17:24,600
Thank you.

507
00:17:24,960 --> 00:17:26,290
Well, that meeting went smoothly.

508
00:17:26,650 --> 00:17:27,470
Better than expected.

509
00:17:27,850 --> 00:17:29,670
Everyone seemed engaged and prepared.

510
00:17:29,990 --> 00:17:32,070
Preparation really makes a difference.

511
00:17:32,090 --> 00:17:32,670
Absolutely.

512
00:17:33,050 --> 00:17:34,320
Do you enjoy leading meetings?

513
00:17:34,800 --> 00:17:35,280
Sometimes.

514
00:17:35,740 --> 00:17:36,740
What's the hardest part?

515
00:17:37,120 --> 00:17:38,020
Managing time.

516
00:17:38,440 --> 00:17:38,940
That's true.

517
00:17:39,340 --> 00:17:41,440
Discussions can easily go off topic.

518
00:17:41,840 --> 00:17:43,620
Especially during brainstorming sessions.

519
00:17:44,110 --> 00:17:44,670
Exactly.

520
00:17:44,990 --> 00:17:48,130
I think strong communication skills are essential for managers.

521
00:17:48,630 --> 00:17:49,110
Definitely.

522
00:17:49,450 --> 00:17:51,390
Good leaders know how to listen as well.

523
00:17:51,510 --> 00:17:53,610
Listening is just as important as speaking.

524
00:17:54,050 --> 00:17:54,530
Absolutely.

525
00:17:54,930 --> 00:17:57,900
Well, I should probably answer my emails before the next meeting.

526
00:17:58,280 --> 00:17:58,740
Same here.

527
00:17:59,100 --> 00:18:00,900
My inbox is completely full.

528
00:18:01,300 --> 00:18:01,790
Mine too.

529
00:18:02,290 --> 00:18:03,770
Office life never slows down.

530
00:18:03,830 --> 00:18:05,130
That's very true.

531
00:18:05,510 --> 00:18:06,210
All right, everyone.

532
00:18:06,390 --> 00:18:08,170
Thank you for practicing English with us today.

533
00:18:08,560 --> 00:18:13,320
We hope these business meeting conversations help you feel more confident in professional situations.

534
00:18:13,760 --> 00:18:17,330
Remember, business English becomes easier with regular practice.

535
00:18:17,350 --> 00:18:19,590
Try repeating these conversations out loud.

536
00:18:19,740 --> 00:18:22,690
You can also practice them with coworkers, classmates, or friends.

537
00:18:23,170 --> 00:18:25,800
The more you speak, the more natural your English will sound.

538
00:18:26,220 --> 00:18:26,720
Keep learning.

539
00:18:27,040 --> 00:18:27,720
Keep practicing.

540
00:18:28,110 --> 00:18:30,550
And keep improving your professional English every day.

541
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:31,640
See you next time.

542
00:18:31,980 --> 00:18:32,620
Goodbye, everyone.

543
00:18:32,920 --> 00:18:33,780
Have a wonderful day.

544
00:19:24,140 --> 00:19:24,940
Hello, everyone.

545
00:19:25,300 --> 00:19:28,640
Welcome back to our English Conversation Practice Podcast.

