Today's schedule looks very busy.

566
00:20:31,620 --> 00:20:32,160
Definitely.

567
00:20:32,340 --> 00:20:35,720
We only have one hour to finalize everything before the client arrives.

568
00:20:36,240 --> 00:20:36,560
I know.

569
00:20:36,620 --> 00:20:39,810
I've already received three emails from the manager this morning.

570
00:20:40,390 --> 00:20:40,890
Same here.

571
00:20:41,210 --> 00:20:43,190
Did you finish updating the sales presentation?

572
00:20:43,730 --> 00:20:44,190
Almost.

573
00:20:44,470 --> 00:20:47,210
I just need to add the latest customer feedback numbers.

574
00:20:47,790 --> 00:20:48,090
Great.

575
00:20:48,290 --> 00:20:51,100
The client specifically asked for updated statistics.

576
00:20:51,400 --> 00:20:52,180
Exactly.

577
00:20:52,480 --> 00:20:55,740
They want to see how customers responded to the new product launch.

578
00:20:56,320 --> 00:20:58,360
Honestly, I think the results look pretty good.

579
00:20:58,850 --> 00:20:59,290
Me too.

580
00:20:59,790 --> 00:21:01,930
Sales increased faster than we expected.

581
00:21:02,370 --> 00:21:03,370
That's always good news.

582
00:21:03,990 --> 00:21:07,070
Unless the finance team starts asking too many questions.

583
00:21:08,380 --> 00:21:08,620
True.

584
00:21:09,120 --> 00:21:11,780
They always want detailed explanations for every number.

585
00:21:12,360 --> 00:21:15,840
Speaking of finance, did Kevin send the final budget report?

586
00:21:16,320 --> 00:21:18,350
Yes, I received it about 10 minutes ago.

587
00:21:18,790 --> 00:21:19,310
Perfect.

588
00:21:19,510 --> 00:21:21,270
That saves us a lot of stress.

589
00:21:21,550 --> 00:21:22,270
Absolutely.

590
00:21:22,570 --> 00:21:25,520
Last week, we almost entered a meeting with incomplete information.

591
00:21:26,020 --> 00:21:26,500
Oh, yes.

592
00:21:26,620 --> 00:21:27,660
That was a disaster.

593
00:21:27,720 --> 00:21:30,040
The manager looked so frustrated.

594
00:21:30,460 --> 00:21:32,700
Especially when the projector stopped working.

595
00:21:32,740 --> 00:21:34,070
Don't remind me.

596
00:21:34,590 --> 00:21:35,790
That meeting felt endless.

597
00:21:36,350 --> 00:21:38,830
Well, hopefully today goes more smoothly.

598
00:21:38,850 --> 00:21:40,130
I hope so, too.

599
00:21:40,630 --> 00:21:43,000
By the way, have you checked the conference room yet?

600
00:21:43,500 --> 00:21:43,940
Not yet.

601
00:21:44,180 --> 00:21:44,400
Why?

602
00:21:44,420 --> 00:21:47,760
I heard another department was using it earlier this morning.

603
00:21:48,300 --> 00:21:48,800
Seriously?

604
00:21:48,840 --> 00:21:51,090
Our meeting starts in less than an hour.

605
00:21:51,320 --> 00:21:51,800
I know.

606
00:21:52,120 --> 00:21:53,780
We should make sure the room is ready.

607
00:21:54,320 --> 00:21:54,820
Good idea.

608
00:21:55,060 --> 00:21:55,980
Let's go check quickly.

609
00:21:56,480 --> 00:21:56,830
Wow.

610
00:21:57,150 --> 00:21:58,810
The room is still full of people.

611
00:21:59,390 --> 00:22:00,050
Excuse me.

612
00:22:00,250 --> 00:22:01,370
Are you almost finished here?

613
00:22:01,950 --> 00:22:02,670
Oh, sorry.

614
00:22:02,890 --> 00:22:04,030
We're wrapping up right now.

615
00:22:04,750 --> 00:22:05,070
Thanks.

616
00:22:05,280 --> 00:22:08,620
We have an important client meeting at 9 a.m. No problem.

617
00:22:08,800 --> 00:22:09,940
We'll leave in five minutes.

618
00:22:10,580 --> 00:22:11,260
Thank goodness.

619
00:22:11,560 --> 00:22:12,360
I was getting nervous.

620
00:22:12,960 --> 00:22:13,540
Same here.

621
00:22:13,920 --> 00:22:16,430
We still need to set up the laptops and documents.

622
00:22:17,050 --> 00:22:18,770
At least the projector's working this time.

623
00:22:19,330 --> 00:22:20,870
Let's hope it stays that way.

624
00:22:21,240 --> 00:22:24,320
All right, while they finish up, let's review the meeting agenda.

625
00:22:24,800 --> 00:22:25,350
Good idea.

626
00:22:25,830 --> 00:22:28,510
First, we'll welcome the client and introduce the team.

627
00:22:29,070 --> 00:22:31,750
Then we'll present the quarterly sales report.

628
00:22:31,780 --> 00:22:35,360
After that, we'll discuss marketing performance and future strategies.

629
00:22:36,000 --> 00:22:38,320
And finally, we'll answer questions from the client.

630
00:22:38,850 --> 00:22:39,890
Sounds simple enough.

631
00:22:40,430 --> 00:22:40,890
Hopefully.

632
00:22:41,230 --> 00:22:43,570
Clients always ask unexpected questions.

633
00:22:44,050 --> 00:22:44,610
That's true.

634
00:22:44,890 --> 00:22:46,340
We should be prepared for anything.

635
00:22:46,860 --> 00:22:49,120
Especially questions about project delays.

636
00:22:49,390 --> 00:22:52,110
Yeah, the production team is still behind schedule.

637
00:22:52,550 --> 00:22:54,790
Do you think the client already knows about the delay?

638
00:22:55,330 --> 00:22:56,010
Probably.

639
00:22:56,030 --> 00:22:59,080
They emailed us twice last week asking for updates.

640
00:22:59,660 --> 00:23:01,540
That could make today's discussion difficult.

641
00:23:02,100 --> 00:23:05,020
Maybe, but honesty is usually the best approach.

642
00:23:05,600 --> 00:23:06,040
I agree.

643
00:23:06,340 --> 00:23:08,900
It's better to explain the problem clearly than hide it.

644
00:23:09,480 --> 00:23:10,110
Exactly.

645
00:23:10,400 --> 00:23:12,190
Clients appreciate transparency.

646
00:23:12,750 --> 00:23:14,450
All right, the room is finally empty.

647
00:23:14,710 --> 00:23:15,890
Let's start setting everything up.

648
00:23:16,410 --> 00:23:18,210
I'll arrange the handouts on the table.

649
00:23:18,440 --> 00:23:18,770
Great.

650
00:23:19,090 --> 00:23:21,230
I'll connect the presentation slides to the projector.

651
00:23:21,650 --> 00:23:23,170
Could you also test the speakers?

652
00:23:23,830 --> 00:23:24,070
Sure.

653
00:23:24,290 --> 00:23:26,350
We'll need them for the product demonstration video.

654
00:23:26,860 --> 00:23:27,170
Thanks.

655
00:23:28,220 --> 00:23:28,300
Hmm.

656
00:23:28,320 --> 00:23:29,800
The sound seems a little low.

657
00:23:30,300 --> 00:23:30,580
Really?

658
00:23:30,620 --> 00:23:31,540
Yeah.

659
00:23:31,600 --> 00:23:33,060
Let me adjust the settings quickly.

660
00:23:33,520 --> 00:23:34,080
Good catch.

661
00:23:34,420 --> 00:23:37,750
Small technical issues can become big problems during meetings.

662
00:23:38,330 --> 00:23:38,850
Exactly.

663
00:23:39,430 --> 00:23:39,970
All right.

664
00:23:40,250 --> 00:23:42,050
I think everything looks ready now.

665
00:23:42,570 --> 00:23:43,230
Perfect timing.

666
00:23:43,450 --> 00:23:44,730
The manager just arrived.

667
00:23:45,260 --> 00:23:45,980
Morning, everyone.

668
00:23:46,240 --> 00:23:47,560
Are we ready for the client meeting?

669
00:23:47,830 --> 00:23:49,430
Yes, almost everything is prepared.

670
00:23:49,890 --> 00:23:50,410
Great work.

671
00:23:50,690 --> 00:23:55,120
We only have 20 minutes left, so let's review the key discussion points quickly.

672
00:23:55,620 --> 00:23:55,840
Sure.

673
00:23:56,420 --> 00:23:59,560
First, we'll highlight the strong sales growth from last quarter.

674
00:24:00,140 --> 00:24:00,380
Right.

675
00:24:00,600 --> 00:24:02,700
The numbers improved by nearly 15%.

676
00:24:02,810 --> 00:24:04,090
Excellent.

677
00:24:04,330 --> 00:24:05,750
That's a strong selling point.

678
00:24:06,170 --> 00:24:08,650
We also prepared customer satisfaction reports.

679
00:24:09,230 --> 00:24:09,490
Good.

680
00:24:09,810 --> 00:24:13,580
The client always focuses heavily on customer experience.

681
00:24:13,830 --> 00:24:16,070
Should we mention the shipping delays immediately?

682
00:24:16,610 --> 00:24:18,090
Yes, but carefully.

683
00:24:18,410 --> 00:24:21,360
We should explain both the problem and our solution.

684
00:24:21,420 --> 00:24:22,600
That makes sense.

685
00:24:23,120 --> 00:24:25,220
We don't want the meeting to sound negative.

686
00:24:25,800 --> 00:24:26,280
Exactly.

687
00:24:26,740 --> 00:24:29,050
Confidence is important during business meetings.

688
00:24:29,650 --> 00:24:30,170
Absolutely.

689
00:24:30,730 --> 00:24:31,350
One more thing.

690
00:24:31,690 --> 00:24:35,970
Please remember to keep your answers short and professional during the Q&A session.

691
00:24:36,560 --> 00:24:36,990
Understood.

692
00:24:37,540 --> 00:24:40,580
Sometimes long explanations create confusion.

693
00:24:40,800 --> 00:24:43,020
especially when clients are short on time.

694
00:24:43,540 --> 00:24:43,980
Correct.

695
00:24:44,560 --> 00:24:46,940
Excuse me, the clients just arrived downstairs.

696
00:24:47,520 --> 00:24:48,340
All right, everyone.

697
00:24:48,400 --> 00:24:50,350
Let's stay calm and professional.

698
00:24:50,850 --> 00:24:51,750
Good morning, everyone.

699
00:24:52,070 --> 00:24:52,930
Welcome to our office.

700
00:24:53,510 --> 00:24:53,970
Thank you.

701
00:24:54,310 --> 00:24:56,650
It's nice to finally meet everyone in person.

702
00:24:57,130 --> 00:24:58,430
Please come in and have a seat.

703
00:24:58,930 --> 00:25:01,480
Would anyone like coffee or tea before we begin?

704
00:25:01,540 --> 00:25:02,780
Coffee would be great.

705
00:25:02,960 --> 00:25:03,300
Thank you.

706
00:25:03,700 --> 00:25:04,160
Of course.

707
00:25:04,740 --> 00:25:05,140
All right.

708
00:25:05,380 --> 00:25:06,600
Let's begin today's meeting.

709
00:25:06,940 --> 00:25:08,310
Thank you all for joining us.

710
00:25:08,540 --> 00:25:12,720
We're excited to discuss the project's progress and future opportunities together.

711
00:25:12,740 --> 00:25:15,360
First, let's quickly introduce ourselves.

712
00:25:15,940 --> 00:25:17,830
I'm Chloe from the marketing department.

713
00:25:18,410 --> 00:25:20,470
And I'm Ethan from sales operations.

714
00:25:20,990 --> 00:25:21,470
Wonderful.

715
00:25:21,830 --> 00:25:24,190
Let's start with the quarterly sales presentation.

716
00:25:24,230 --> 00:25:24,830
Ethan.

717
00:25:25,350 --> 00:25:25,730
Thank you.

718
00:25:26,430 --> 00:25:30,100
Over the past three months, sales performance exceeded our expectations.

719
00:25:30,680 --> 00:25:31,500
That's great to hear.

720
00:25:31,560 --> 00:25:36,500
Online sales increased significantly after the launch of our new advertising campaign.

721
00:25:36,750 --> 00:25:38,840
Which marketing channels performed best?

722
00:25:39,500 --> 00:25:42,760
Short-form video advertisements generated the highest engagement.

723
00:25:43,260 --> 00:25:43,760
Interesting.

724
00:25:44,040 --> 00:25:45,680
That matches current market trends.

725
00:25:46,210 --> 00:25:46,730
Exactly.

726
00:25:47,010 --> 00:25:50,790
We also noticed increased customer interaction on social media platforms.

727
00:25:51,310 --> 00:25:51,790
Excellent.

728
00:25:52,330 --> 00:25:56,060
However, we did face some shipping delays during peak order periods.

729
00:25:56,600 --> 00:25:59,340
Yes, we noticed some complaints from customers.

730
00:25:59,960 --> 00:26:01,970
We completely understand your concern.

731
00:26:02,220 --> 00:26:06,680
The delays were caused by supplier shortages and increased seasonal demand.

732
00:26:07,320 --> 00:26:07,740
I see.

733
00:26:07,780 --> 00:26:10,420
What steps are you taking to improve the situation?

734
00:26:10,850 --> 00:26:15,110
We're currently expanding warehouse support and improving delivery coordination.

735
00:26:15,590 --> 00:26:18,830
We also hired temporary staff to reduce processing times.

736
00:26:19,390 --> 00:26:20,430
That sounds reassuring.

737
00:26:20,840 --> 00:26:24,860
We expect delivery performance to improve significantly within the next month.

738
00:26:25,400 --> 00:26:25,800
Excellent.

739
00:26:26,040 --> 00:26:29,200
Communication and transparency are very important to us.

740
00:26:29,390 --> 00:26:30,630
We completely agree.

741
00:26:30,670 --> 00:26:33,790
Now let's discuss future expansion plans.

742
00:26:34,370 --> 00:26:37,910
We're planning to focus more heavily on international markets next year.

743
00:26:38,380 --> 00:26:39,120
That's exciting.

744
00:26:39,600 --> 00:26:41,420
Which regions are you targeting first?

745
00:26:41,960 --> 00:26:46,140
We're currently researching opportunities in Southeast Asia and Europe.

746
00:26:46,160 --> 00:26:48,630
Those markets have strong growth potential right now.

747
00:26:49,130 --> 00:26:49,650
Exactly.

748
00:26:49,950 --> 00:26:51,730
We believe there's strong demand there.

749
00:26:52,250 --> 00:26:54,130
Have you considered local partnerships?

750
00:26:54,710 --> 00:26:58,180
Yes, we're already in discussions with several regional distributors.

751
00:26:58,410 --> 00:26:59,050
Very good.

752
00:26:59,370 --> 00:27:01,330
That should help market entry significantly.

753
00:27:01,790 --> 00:27:02,430
That's our goal.

754
00:27:02,990 --> 00:27:05,740
Does anyone have additional questions before we wrap up?

755
00:27:06,280 --> 00:27:09,280
I'd like to ask about the timeline for the next product release.

756
00:27:09,800 --> 00:27:10,220
Of course.

757
00:27:10,540 --> 00:27:12,220
We're aiming for early September.

758
00:27:12,810 --> 00:27:13,070
Great.

759
00:27:13,370 --> 00:27:15,370
We'll prepare our marketing schedule accordingly.

760
00:27:15,850 --> 00:27:16,290
Wonderful.

761
00:27:16,790 --> 00:27:18,410
Thank you everyone for your time today.

762
00:27:18,890 --> 00:27:20,950
We appreciate the opportunity to work together.

763
00:27:21,430 --> 00:27:21,870
Thank you.

764
00:27:22,150 --> 00:27:23,660
This meeting was very productive.

765
00:27:24,220 --> 00:27:26,040
We look forward to future collaboration.

766
00:27:26,240 --> 00:27:27,440
Well done, Chloe.

767
00:27:27,620 --> 00:27:29,080
That meeting went really well.

768
00:27:29,620 --> 00:27:29,940
Thanks.

769
00:27:30,360 --> 00:27:32,130
Everyone stayed calm and professional.

770
00:27:32,750 --> 00:27:35,530
And thankfully, there were no technical disasters this time.

771
00:27:36,370 --> 00:27:39,300
Yes, that alone feels like a huge success.

772
00:27:39,840 --> 00:27:42,560
I think the clients were happy with our honesty about the delays.

773
00:27:43,060 --> 00:27:43,600
Definitely.

774
00:27:43,960 --> 00:27:46,400
Clear communication builds trust.

775
00:27:46,420 --> 00:27:46,740
Agreed.

776
00:27:47,230 --> 00:27:50,290
You also handled the difficult questions very confidently.

777
00:27:50,770 --> 00:27:51,090
Thanks.

778
00:27:51,630 --> 00:27:53,110
I was nervous at first, honestly.

779
00:27:53,630 --> 00:27:53,950
Really?

780
00:27:53,990 --> 00:27:55,860
You looked completely relaxed.

781
00:27:56,140 --> 00:27:59,410
That's because I practiced my presentation several times this morning.

782
00:27:59,850 --> 00:28:01,810
Preparation makes a huge difference.

783
00:28:02,410 --> 00:28:02,910
Absolutely.

784
00:28:03,470 --> 00:28:07,040
Well, after that stressful hour, I think we deserve coffee.

785
00:28:07,700 --> 00:28:09,380
I completely agree with that idea.

786
00:28:09,930 --> 00:28:12,290
Let's grab coffee before the next meeting starts.

787
00:28:12,890 --> 00:28:14,390
Wait, there's another meeting today?

788
00:28:14,910 --> 00:28:16,420
Welcome to office life, even.

789
00:28:16,500 --> 00:28:18,520
Fair enough.

790
00:28:18,820 --> 00:28:19,360
Let's go.

791
00:28:19,550 --> 00:28:20,410
All right, everyone.

792
00:28:20,450 --> 00:28:26,530
We hope you enjoyed today's English conversation practice about business meeting conversations in 60 minutes.

793
00:28:27,090 --> 00:28:34,340
Today, we practiced useful English for presentations, teamwork, client meetings, problem solving, and office communication.

794
00:28:34,860 --> 00:28:39,010
These are real expressions you can use in professional situations every day.

795
00:28:39,070 --> 00:28:43,290
Remember, confidence comes through regular practice and communication.

796
00:28:43,710 --> 00:28:48,460
Keep practicing your English step by step, and don't be afraid to speak during meetings.

797
00:28:48,570 --> 00:28:50,720
Thanks so much for learning with us today.

798
00:28:51,160 --> 00:28:54,310
We'll see you again in the next English conversation practice session.

799
00:28:54,790 --> 00:28:55,590
Take care, everyone.

800
00:28:56,090 --> 00:28:58,700
And keep improving your English every single day.

801
00:30:04,120 --> 00:30:04,900
Hello, everyone.

802
00:30:05,100 --> 00:30:07,380
Welcome back to our English Learning Podcast.

803
00:30:07,800 --> 00:30:09,410
We're so happy you joined us today.

804
00:30:09,910 --> 00:30:10,430
I'm Ryan.

805
00:30:10,750 --> 00:30:11,470
And I'm Chloe.

806
00:30:11,870 --> 00:30:16,270
Today we have another practical English lesson for office workers and business professionals.

807
00:30:16,750 --> 00:30:17,190
That's right.

808
00:30:17,600 --> 00:30:21,580
Today's topic is business meeting conversations in 60 minutes.

809
00:30:22,160 --> 00:30:24,840
In many companies, meetings are scheduled for one hour.

810
00:30:25,340 --> 00:30:31,950
During that time, people discuss projects, solve problems, give updates, make decisions, and share ideas.

811
00:30:32,100 --> 00:30:37,720
So today we'll practice realistic business conversations that happen during a typical one-hour office meeting.

812
00:30:38,140 --> 00:30:46,850
You'll learn useful English phrases for starting meetings, presenting ideas, discussing deadlines, handling disagreements, and ending meetings professionally.

813
00:30:47,330 --> 00:30:47,970
And don't worry.

814
00:30:48,320 --> 00:30:51,680
We'll use clear and natural English so you can follow along easily.

815
00:30:52,200 --> 00:30:52,560
All right.

816
00:30:53,040 --> 00:30:53,480
Let's begin.

817
00:30:53,920 --> 00:30:54,660
Good morning, Chloe.

818
00:30:54,980 --> 00:30:55,720
Good morning, Ryan.

819
00:30:55,960 --> 00:30:56,920
You're here early today.

820
00:30:57,400 --> 00:31:00,030
I wanted to prepare the conference room before the team arrived.

821
00:31:00,410 --> 00:31:01,450
That's responsible.

822
00:31:01,490 --> 00:31:02,740
Today's meeting is important.

823
00:31:03,140 --> 00:31:03,680
Definitely.

824
00:31:04,060 --> 00:31:06,700
The management team wants updates on every department.

825
00:31:07,080 --> 00:31:08,920
I heard the CEO might join the meeting too.

826
00:31:09,300 --> 00:31:09,600
Really?

827
00:31:09,620 --> 00:31:10,280
Yes.

828
00:31:10,680 --> 00:31:12,810
Then we should make sure everything is organized.

829
00:31:13,210 --> 00:31:13,510
Agreed.

830
00:31:13,930 --> 00:31:15,550
Did you print the presentation handouts?

831
00:31:16,010 --> 00:31:18,270
Yes, I printed enough copies for everyone.

832
00:31:18,610 --> 00:31:19,010
Perfect.

833
00:31:19,470 --> 00:31:21,690
I also prepared coffee and water for the meeting.

834
00:31:22,140 --> 00:31:22,880
Excellent planning.

835
00:31:23,220 --> 00:31:23,520
Thanks.

836
00:31:24,040 --> 00:31:25,700
By the way, how was your commute this morning?

837
00:31:26,100 --> 00:31:27,080
Surprisingly smooth.

838
00:31:27,460 --> 00:31:28,020
Lucky you.

839
00:31:28,480 --> 00:31:29,480
Traffic was bad for you?

840
00:31:29,920 --> 00:31:30,440
Terrible.

841
00:31:30,820 --> 00:31:31,480
What happened?

842
00:31:31,700 --> 00:31:33,360
There was construction near the highway.

843
00:31:33,780 --> 00:31:34,510
That explains it.

844
00:31:34,890 --> 00:31:36,690
I spent almost an hour in traffic.

845
00:31:37,090 --> 00:31:38,190
That sounds exhausting.

846
