982
00:35:47,810 --> 00:35:50,050
Several teams have been working overtime recently.

983
00:35:50,470 --> 00:35:51,790
Yes, I've noticed that.

984
00:35:52,210 --> 00:35:53,910
Employee stress levels are increasing.

985
00:35:54,280 --> 00:35:55,080
That's concerning.

986
00:35:55,520 --> 00:35:58,080
Burnout can affect both productivity and morale.

987
00:35:58,500 --> 00:35:59,480
I completely agree.

988
00:35:59,860 --> 00:36:01,080
Do you have any suggestions?

989
00:36:01,560 --> 00:36:04,590
We could redistribute tasks more evenly between teams.

990
00:36:05,070 --> 00:36:05,570
Good idea.

991
00:36:05,950 --> 00:36:08,570
We might also consider hiring temporary staff.

992
00:36:08,820 --> 00:36:10,970
That could reduce pressure during busy periods.

993
00:36:11,450 --> 00:36:11,950
Exactly.

994
00:36:12,370 --> 00:36:13,910
Another issue is communication.

995
00:36:14,330 --> 00:36:15,830
What kind of communication problems?

996
00:36:16,330 --> 00:36:18,800
Some employees feel uncomfortable asking for help.

997
00:36:19,200 --> 00:36:21,340
That happens often in stressful environments.

998
00:36:21,800 --> 00:36:23,960
Managers should encourage open communication.

999
00:36:24,440 --> 00:36:24,960
Definitely.

1000
00:36:25,360 --> 00:36:26,870
Team members should feel supported.

1001
00:36:27,290 --> 00:36:27,730
I agree.

1002
00:36:28,110 --> 00:36:31,750
We could also organize wellness workshops or stress management sessions.

1003
00:36:32,170 --> 00:36:33,270
That's an excellent idea.

1004
00:36:33,670 --> 00:36:35,460
Mental health is important in the workplace.

1005
00:36:36,020 --> 00:36:36,840
Absolutely.

1006
00:36:36,890 --> 00:36:39,610
All right, now let's discuss future company goals.

1007
00:36:40,250 --> 00:36:42,870
One major goal is expanding into international markets.

1008
00:36:43,370 --> 00:36:43,810
Exciting.

1009
00:36:44,190 --> 00:36:46,910
We're currently researching opportunities in Europe and Asia.

1010
00:36:47,300 --> 00:36:48,940
That could create significant growth.

1011
00:36:49,380 --> 00:36:49,880
Exactly.

1012
00:36:50,320 --> 00:36:51,720
What challenges do you expect?

1013
00:36:52,180 --> 00:36:54,340
Cultural differences and local competition.

1014
00:36:54,700 --> 00:36:55,940
Those are important factors.

1015
00:36:56,400 --> 00:36:59,190
We'll need strong market research before making decisions.

1016
00:36:59,690 --> 00:37:00,150
Definitely.

1017
00:37:00,650 --> 00:37:03,190
Another goal is improving sustainability practices.

1018
00:37:03,630 --> 00:37:06,670
Customers care more about environmental responsibility now.

1019
00:37:06,940 --> 00:37:07,560
Very true.

1020
00:37:07,960 --> 00:37:09,300
What changes are we considering?

1021
00:37:09,740 --> 00:37:12,490
Reducing paper waste and improving energy efficiency.

1022
00:37:12,840 --> 00:37:13,550
Good initiatives.

1023
00:37:14,010 --> 00:37:16,550
We also want to work with more eco-friendly suppliers.

1024
00:37:17,050 --> 00:37:18,970
That would strengthen the company's reputation.

1025
00:37:19,410 --> 00:37:19,910
Exactly.

1026
00:37:20,310 --> 00:37:24,110
All right, before we finish, does anyone have additional comments or questions?

1027
00:37:24,610 --> 00:37:27,040
I have one question regarding remote work policies.

1028
00:37:27,440 --> 00:37:27,840
Go ahead.

1029
00:37:28,260 --> 00:37:30,740
Will employees continue working from home part-time?

1030
00:37:31,140 --> 00:37:31,960
At the moment, yes.

1031
00:37:32,420 --> 00:37:33,080
That's good news.

1032
00:37:33,480 --> 00:37:36,850
Management believes flexible work schedules improve productivity.

1033
00:37:36,890 --> 00:37:37,930
I agree completely.

1034
00:37:38,260 --> 00:37:41,180
However, teams still need regular in-person meetings.

1035
00:37:41,700 --> 00:37:42,060
Of course.

1036
00:37:42,540 --> 00:37:45,530
Face-to-face communication remains important for collaboration.

1037
00:37:45,990 --> 00:37:46,490
Definitely.

1038
00:37:46,890 --> 00:37:47,650
Any other questions?

1039
00:37:48,240 --> 00:37:48,800
Nothing from me.

1040
00:37:49,200 --> 00:37:49,520
All right.

1041
00:37:49,920 --> 00:37:51,300
Then let's wrap up today's meeting.

1042
00:37:51,640 --> 00:37:54,250
Thank you everyone for your hard work and participation.

1043
00:37:54,610 --> 00:37:57,090
Please send your updated reports by Friday afternoon.

1044
00:37:57,570 --> 00:37:59,900
And don't forget next week's strategy meeting.

1045
00:38:00,010 --> 00:38:01,270
Have a productive day, everyone.

1046
00:38:01,610 --> 00:38:01,990
Thank you.

1047
00:38:02,360 --> 00:38:03,700
Well, that meeting went smoothly.

1048
00:38:04,060 --> 00:38:04,880
Better than expected.

1049
00:38:05,240 --> 00:38:07,040
Everyone seemed engaged and prepared.

1050
00:38:07,380 --> 00:38:09,000
Preparation really makes a difference.

1051
00:38:09,500 --> 00:38:10,060
Absolutely.

1052
00:38:10,470 --> 00:38:11,730
Do you enjoy leading meetings?

1053
00:38:12,210 --> 00:38:12,690
Sometimes.

1054
00:38:13,150 --> 00:38:14,490
What's the hardest part?

1055
00:38:14,510 --> 00:38:15,410
Managing time.

1056
00:38:15,830 --> 00:38:16,350
That's true.

1057
00:38:16,730 --> 00:38:18,840
Discussions can easily go off topic.

1058
00:38:19,240 --> 00:38:21,020
Especially during brainstorming sessions.

1059
00:38:21,520 --> 00:38:22,080
Exactly.

1060
00:38:22,400 --> 00:38:25,540
I think strong communication skills are essential for managers.

1061
00:38:26,020 --> 00:38:26,520
Definitely.

1062
00:38:26,840 --> 00:38:28,790
Good leaders know how to listen as well.

1063
00:38:28,900 --> 00:38:31,010
Listening is just as important as speaking.

1064
00:38:31,470 --> 00:38:31,950
Absolutely.

1065
00:38:32,350 --> 00:38:35,290
Well, I should probably answer my emails before the next meeting.

1066
00:38:35,690 --> 00:38:36,150
Same here.

1067
00:38:36,490 --> 00:38:38,300
My inbox is completely full.

1068
00:38:38,700 --> 00:38:39,180
Mine too.

1069
00:38:39,680 --> 00:38:41,160
Office life never slows down.

1070
00:38:41,220 --> 00:38:42,520
That's very true.

1071
00:38:42,900 --> 00:38:43,620
All right, everyone.

1072
00:38:43,780 --> 00:38:45,570
Thank you for practicing English with us today.

1073
00:38:45,950 --> 00:38:50,720
We hope these business meeting conversations help you feel more confident in professional situations.

1074
00:38:51,180 --> 00:38:54,740
Remember, business English becomes easier with regular practice.

1075
00:38:54,760 --> 00:38:56,990
Try repeating these conversations out loud.

1076
00:38:57,130 --> 00:39:00,080
You can also practice them with co-workers, classmates, or friends.

1077
00:39:00,560 --> 00:39:03,210
The more you speak, the more natural your English will sound.

1078
00:39:03,610 --> 00:39:04,110
Keep learning.

1079
00:39:04,430 --> 00:39:05,120
Keep practicing.

1080
00:39:05,520 --> 00:39:07,950
And keep improving your professional English every day.

1081
00:39:08,410 --> 00:39:09,050
See you next time.

1082
00:39:09,370 --> 00:39:10,010
Goodbye, everyone.

1083
00:39:10,330 --> 00:39:11,190
Have a wonderful day.

1084
00:40:27,640 --> 00:40:31,840
Hello, everyone, and welcome back to our English conversation practice session.

1085
00:40:32,180 --> 00:40:32,620
I'm Ethan.

1086
00:40:33,040 --> 00:40:33,620
And I'm Mia.

1087
00:40:34,010 --> 00:40:36,570
We're so happy you're here learning English with us today.

1088
00:40:36,930 --> 00:40:42,100
If you want to improve your spoken English for work and professional situations, you're in the right place.

1089
00:40:42,540 --> 00:40:42,940
That's right.

1090
00:40:43,340 --> 00:40:47,090
Today's topic is business meeting conversations in 60 minutes.

1091
00:40:47,630 --> 00:40:53,680
We're going to practice realistic office conversations that happen before, during, and after business meetings.

1092
00:40:53,840 --> 00:41:01,450
You'll hear useful phrases for presenting ideas, discussing problems, asking questions, sharing opinions, and working with a team.

1093
00:41:01,970 --> 00:41:07,560
And just like always, we'll use clear and natural English that sounds professional but easy to understand.

1094
00:41:08,000 --> 00:41:10,760
All right, Ethan, are you ready to start today's meeting practice?

1095
00:41:11,320 --> 00:41:11,880
Absolutely.

1096
00:41:12,020 --> 00:41:12,560
Let's begin.

1097
00:41:12,970 --> 00:41:13,790
Good morning, Ethan.

1098
00:41:14,010 --> 00:41:15,730
You're here earlier than usual today.

1099
00:41:16,110 --> 00:41:16,670
Morning, Mia.

1100
00:41:16,990 --> 00:41:19,930
Yeah, I wanted to prepare before the strategy meeting starts.

1101
00:41:20,130 --> 00:41:20,730
Same here.

1102
00:41:20,930 --> 00:41:22,700
Today's meeting sounds pretty important.

1103
00:41:23,040 --> 00:41:23,540
Definitely.

1104
00:41:24,020 --> 00:41:26,520
