Charts usually explain things faster.

1126
00:42:02,310 --> 00:42:02,810
Exactly.

1127
00:42:03,150 --> 00:42:05,390
Especially during meetings where time is limited.

1128
00:42:05,870 --> 00:42:09,920
Speaking of time, this meeting is scheduled for exactly 60 minutes.

1129
00:42:10,480 --> 00:42:13,760
That means everyone needs to keep their updates short and clear.

1130
00:42:13,850 --> 00:42:16,230
which is honestly harder than it sounds.

1131
00:42:16,810 --> 00:42:17,430
Very true.

1132
00:42:17,910 --> 00:42:21,280
Some people turn five-minute updates into 20-minute speeches.

1133
00:42:22,740 --> 00:42:24,160
We all know who you're talking about.

1134
00:42:24,730 --> 00:42:25,830
I'm not naming names.

1135
00:42:26,350 --> 00:42:26,690
All right.

1136
00:42:26,750 --> 00:42:28,030
Should we go to the conference room?

1137
00:42:28,450 --> 00:42:28,690
Sure.

1138
00:42:28,850 --> 00:42:30,100
Let's grab coffee first, though.

1139
00:42:30,420 --> 00:42:31,740
I'll need extra energy today.

1140
00:42:32,240 --> 00:42:32,900
Same here.

1141
00:42:33,070 --> 00:42:34,070
Good morning, everyone.

1142
00:42:34,310 --> 00:42:36,850
Thanks for joining today's business meeting conversation.

1143
00:42:37,190 --> 00:42:37,670
Good morning.

1144
00:42:38,130 --> 00:42:38,820
Morning, everyone.

1145
00:42:39,220 --> 00:42:42,000
Since we only have 60 minutes, let's begin right away.

1146
00:42:42,400 --> 00:42:42,900
Good idea.

1147
00:42:43,340 --> 00:42:46,110
First, we'll review project progress from each department.

1148
00:42:46,450 --> 00:42:48,670
Then we'll discuss next month's goals.

1149
00:42:48,690 --> 00:42:49,150
Sounds good.

1150
00:42:49,610 --> 00:42:51,690
Ethan, would you like to start with the marketing update?

1151
00:42:52,150 --> 00:42:52,550
Of course.

1152
00:42:53,050 --> 00:42:56,320
Over the past month, our online engagement increased by 12%.

1153
00:42:56,680 --> 00:42:58,140
That's excellent news.

1154
00:42:58,600 --> 00:43:00,200
What contributed to the increase?

1155
00:43:00,350 --> 00:43:04,460
mainly short-form video campaigns and stronger social media interaction.

1156
00:43:04,860 --> 00:43:05,320
Interesting.

1157
00:43:05,620 --> 00:43:07,180
Which platform performed best?

1158
00:43:07,700 --> 00:43:10,200
Instagram generated the highest audience engagement.

1159
00:43:10,540 --> 00:43:11,200
That makes sense.

1160
00:43:11,450 --> 00:43:13,870
Video content is extremely popular right now.

1161
00:43:14,330 --> 00:43:14,850
Exactly.

1162
00:43:15,210 --> 00:43:19,050
We also noticed customers responding positively to behind-the-scenes content.

1163
00:43:19,410 --> 00:43:20,640
That's valuable information.

1164
00:43:21,110 --> 00:43:24,080
However, email campaign performance dropped slightly.

1165
00:43:24,440 --> 00:43:25,100
Do we know why?

1166
00:43:25,140 --> 00:43:28,180
We believe the messages were too long and formal.

1167
00:43:28,300 --> 00:43:28,880
I agree.

1168
00:43:28,940 --> 00:43:32,740
Usually, customers prefer shorter and more personal communication.

1169
00:43:33,200 --> 00:43:35,010
That's what our research suggests as well.

1170
00:43:35,490 --> 00:43:37,010
So, what changes are you planning?

1171
00:43:37,410 --> 00:43:41,790
We'd like to redesign the email format and focus more on personalized messaging.

1172
00:43:42,280 --> 00:43:43,400
Sounds like a smart approach.

1173
00:43:43,860 --> 00:43:44,180
Thank you.

1174
00:43:44,620 --> 00:43:47,160
All right, let's move on to the sales department update.

1175
00:43:47,500 --> 00:43:48,300
Good morning, everyone.

1176
00:43:48,800 --> 00:43:51,630
Overall sales increased by 8% this quarter.

1177
00:43:52,010 --> 00:43:52,730
Great progress.

1178
00:43:53,230 --> 00:43:53,550
Thank you.

1179
00:43:54,050 --> 00:43:57,290
However, we faced delays in two major client projects.

1180
00:43:57,490 --> 00:43:58,670
What caused the delays?

1181
00:43:59,230 --> 00:44:02,080
Mostly supply chain issues and late product deliveries.

1182
00:44:02,560 --> 00:44:03,920
Are those issues resolved now?

1183
00:44:04,500 --> 00:44:07,760
Mostly, yes, but we're still monitoring the situation carefully.

1184
00:44:08,110 --> 00:44:08,370
Good.

1185
00:44:08,590 --> 00:44:11,510
Keeping clients informed is very important during delays.

1186
00:44:12,090 --> 00:44:12,690
Absolutely.

1187
00:44:13,090 --> 00:44:15,270
Communication helped us avoid bigger problems.

1188
00:44:15,740 --> 00:44:17,600
Did any clients react negatively?

1189
00:44:18,040 --> 00:44:22,600
A few were frustrated at first, but they appreciated our honesty and regular updates.

1190
00:44:23,080 --> 00:44:26,370
Transparency is always important in business relationships.

1191
00:44:26,590 --> 00:44:27,730
I completely agree.

1192
00:44:28,190 --> 00:44:28,570
Excellent.

1193
00:44:28,710 --> 00:44:29,570
Thank you for the update.

1194
00:44:29,970 --> 00:44:31,590
Excuse me, may I add something?

1195
00:44:31,990 --> 00:44:32,370
Of course.

1196
00:44:32,530 --> 00:44:32,950
Go ahead.

1197
00:44:33,380 --> 00:44:36,880
I think departments should communicate more frequently during large projects.

1198
00:44:37,360 --> 00:44:38,480
What do you mean exactly?

1199
00:44:38,980 --> 00:44:43,810
Sometimes marketing, sales, and operations work separately without sharing enough information.

1200
00:44:44,190 --> 00:44:45,710
That's actually a very good point.

1201
00:44:46,170 --> 00:44:49,460
Better communication could help us avoid delays and misunderstandings.

1202
00:44:49,900 --> 00:44:50,740
I agree completely.

1203
00:44:51,220 --> 00:44:54,060
Maybe we could organize shorter weekly communication meetings.

1204
00:44:54,510 --> 00:44:55,970
That sounds like a great idea.

1205
00:44:56,010 --> 00:44:57,240
It wouldn't need to be long.

1206
00:44:57,280 --> 00:44:59,560
Even 15 minutes could help.

1207
00:44:59,580 --> 00:45:01,020
That sounds practical and efficient.

1208
00:45:01,460 --> 00:45:02,540
Great suggestion, Ethan.

1209
00:45:02,880 --> 00:45:03,200
Thanks.

1210
00:45:03,740 --> 00:45:04,420
All right, everyone.

1211
00:45:04,800 --> 00:45:06,490
Let's discuss next month's goals.

1212
00:45:07,010 --> 00:45:11,190
The company wants to improve customer satisfaction and internal communication.

1213
00:45:11,670 --> 00:45:13,370
Those are both important priorities.

1214
00:45:13,870 --> 00:45:14,390
Exactly.

1215
00:45:14,750 --> 00:45:18,740
We also want to reduce project delays by improving workflow efficiency.

1216
00:45:19,200 --> 00:45:21,900
That will require stronger teamwork across departments.

1217
00:45:22,420 --> 00:45:23,220
Absolutely.

1218
00:45:23,280 --> 00:45:25,410
I have a question about the new workflow system.

1219
00:45:25,870 --> 00:45:26,110
Sure.

1220
00:45:26,490 --> 00:45:29,170
Will employees receive training before implementation?

1221
00:45:29,590 --> 00:45:29,870
Yes.

1222
00:45:30,110 --> 00:45:32,110
Training sessions will begin next Monday.

1223
00:45:32,470 --> 00:45:32,700
Good.

1224
00:45:32,970 --> 00:45:34,400
That should make the transition easier.

1225
00:45:34,840 --> 00:45:37,460
We want everyone to feel comfortable using the new system.

1226
00:45:37,920 --> 00:45:38,600
That's important.

1227
00:45:39,080 --> 00:45:40,940
Sudden changes can create confusion.

1228
00:45:41,380 --> 00:45:41,900
Exactly.

1229
00:45:42,360 --> 00:45:45,010
By the way, do we know when the software upgrade will happen?

1230
00:45:45,430 --> 00:45:48,370
IT plans to complete installation by the end of the month.

1231
00:45:48,830 --> 00:45:49,230
Perfect.

1232
00:45:49,570 --> 00:45:52,740
We'll also provide technical support during the first few weeks.

1233
00:45:52,930 --> 00:45:57,400
That's reassuring, especially for employees who aren't very comfortable with technology yet.

1234
00:45:58,640 --> 00:45:59,940
I know a few people like that.

1235
00:46:00,500 --> 00:46:02,180
I think every office has them.

1236
00:46:02,200 --> 00:46:02,520
True.

1237
00:46:02,960 --> 00:46:05,430
All right, everyone, we still have 20 minutes left.

1238
00:46:05,470 --> 00:46:07,590
Let's open the floor for questions and ideas.

1239
00:46:08,150 --> 00:46:10,830
I'd like to suggest something regarding team productivity.

1240
00:46:11,170 --> 00:46:11,590
Go ahead.

1241
00:46:11,990 --> 00:46:15,150
I think too many long meetings reduce efficiency sometimes.

1242
00:46:15,590 --> 00:46:16,340
Interesting point.

1243
00:46:16,860 --> 00:46:20,700
Some meetings could probably be shorter or handled through email updates instead.

1244
00:46:21,100 --> 00:46:22,620
Honestly, I agree with that.

1245
00:46:22,750 --> 00:46:26,320
People lose focus when meetings last too long without clear goals.

1246
00:46:26,860 --> 00:46:27,440
Very true.

1247
00:46:27,920 --> 00:46:30,740
Maybe we should create stricter meeting schedules and agendas.

1248
00:46:31,180 --> 00:46:32,860
That would help everyone stay organized.

1249
00:46:33,320 --> 00:46:33,840
Exactly.

1250
00:46:34,260 --> 00:46:38,510
I think shorter meetings with clear action points would improve productivity significantly.

1251
00:46:38,930 --> 00:46:39,550
Great idea.

1252
00:46:39,910 --> 00:46:42,880
We should also encourage employees to prepare before meetings.

1253
00:46:43,400 --> 00:46:46,280
Preparation saves a lot of time.

1254
00:46:46,380 --> 00:46:47,680
I have another suggestion.

1255
00:46:48,140 --> 00:46:48,440
Sure.

1256
00:46:48,900 --> 00:46:51,520
Maybe we could organize monthly team building activities.

1257
00:46:51,960 --> 00:46:52,660
That sounds fun.

1258
00:46:53,190 --> 00:46:57,670
Better relationships between coworkers often improve communication and teamwork.

1259
00:46:57,690 --> 00:46:58,550
I completely agree.

1260
00:46:58,990 --> 00:47:00,820
What kind of activities are you thinking about?

1261
00:47:01,260 --> 00:47:05,100
Maybe group lunches, outdoor events, or problem solving games.

1262
00:47:05,640 --> 00:47:07,000
Escape rooms could be interesting.

1263
00:47:07,540 --> 00:47:09,270
Oh, that would actually be really fun.

1264
00:47:09,690 --> 00:47:12,610
Plus, they require teamwork and communication skills.

1265
00:47:12,630 --> 00:47:13,430
Exactly.

1266
00:47:13,580 --> 00:47:14,380
All right, everyone.

1267
00:47:14,620 --> 00:47:17,320
Before we finish, let's review today's action points.

1268
00:47:17,820 --> 00:47:21,470
First, the marketing team will redesign the email campaign strategy.

1269
00:47:21,930 --> 00:47:25,250
Second, departments will begin shorter weekly communication meetings.

1270
00:47:25,650 --> 00:47:29,320
Third, employee training for the new workflow system starts Monday.

1271
00:47:29,740 --> 00:47:33,780
And finally, management will discuss ideas for future team-building activities.

1272
00:47:34,240 --> 00:47:34,940
Perfect summary.

1273
00:47:35,320 --> 00:47:38,010
Does anyone have final questions before we end today's meeting?

1274
00:47:38,430 --> 00:47:39,050
Nothing from me.

1275
00:47:39,530 --> 00:47:40,330
I'm good, too.

1276
00:47:40,480 --> 00:47:41,000
All right then.

1277
00:47:41,240 --> 00:47:43,880
Thank you, everyone, for your time and participation today.

1278
00:47:44,320 --> 00:47:44,680
Thank you.

1279
00:47:44,720 --> 00:47:45,700
Thanks, everyone.

1280
00:47:46,110 --> 00:47:47,290
Great meeting today, Mia.

1281
00:47:47,630 --> 00:47:47,950
Thanks.

1282
00:47:48,230 --> 00:47:49,650
I think everything went smoothly.

1283
00:47:50,110 --> 00:47:52,230
And we actually finished within 60 minutes.

1284
00:47:52,690 --> 00:47:54,610
That might be the most impressive part.

1285
00:47:55,460 --> 00:47:55,980
Very true.

1286
00:47:56,020 --> 00:47:59,180
Honestly, shorter meetings feel much more productive.

1287
00:47:59,740 --> 00:48:00,660
I agree completely.

1288
00:48:01,060 --> 00:48:03,430
People stay focused when discussions are organized.

1289
00:48:03,850 --> 00:48:04,390
Exactly.

1290
00:48:04,870 --> 00:48:07,430
I also liked hearing ideas from different departments.

1291
00:48:07,680 --> 00:48:08,260
Same here.

1292
00:48:08,620 --> 00:48:11,510
Cross-department communication is really important.

1293
00:48:11,530 --> 00:48:12,030
Definitely.

1294
00:48:12,550 --> 00:48:15,130
Sometimes teams become too isolated from each other.

1295
00:48:15,550 --> 00:48:17,430
And that creates misunderstandings later.

1296
00:48:17,950 --> 00:48:18,510
Exactly.

1297
00:48:19,130 --> 00:48:22,180
By the way, your suggestion about shorter meetings was excellent.

1298
00:48:22,560 --> 00:48:23,200
Thanks.

1299
00:48:23,220 --> 00:48:25,240
I've honestly been thinking about it for months.

1300
00:48:26,400 --> 00:48:26,860
I could tell.

1301
00:48:27,340 --> 00:48:28,420
What about your presentation?

1302
00:48:28,460 --> 00:48:30,120
You looked very confident today.

1303
00:48:30,530 --> 00:48:30,790
Really?

1304
00:48:31,130 --> 00:48:32,610
I was nervous before speaking.

1305
00:48:32,690 --> 00:48:34,130
Honestly, nobody could tell.

1306
00:48:34,610 --> 00:48:35,270
That's good to hear.

1307
00:48:35,790 --> 00:48:38,020
Your explanations were very clear and professional.

1308
00:48:38,420 --> 00:48:38,760
Thanks.

1309
00:48:38,980 --> 00:48:40,320
I practiced a lot last night.

1310
00:48:40,720 --> 00:48:42,020
Practice definitely helps.

1311
00:48:42,520 --> 00:48:43,220
It really does.

1312
00:48:43,740 --> 00:48:44,950
Hey, are you free for lunch now?

1313
00:48:45,390 --> 00:48:45,910
Absolutely.

1314
00:48:45,950 --> 00:48:47,510
I'm starving after that meeting.

1315
00:48:48,010 --> 00:48:48,290
Same.

1316
00:48:48,730 --> 00:48:50,430
My brain needs food immediately.

1317
00:48:51,630 --> 00:48:52,750
Let's invite the others, too.

1318
00:48:53,240 --> 00:48:53,720
Good idea.

1319
00:48:53,760 --> 00:48:55,540
Team lunches are always fun.

1320
00:48:55,900 --> 00:48:59,320
Plus, people communicate more naturally outside formal meetings.

1321
00:48:59,370 --> 00:48:59,950
That's true.

1322
00:49:00,510 --> 00:49:03,470
Some of the best ideas happen during casual conversations.

1323
00:49:03,980 --> 00:49:04,460
Exactly.

1324
00:49:04,960 --> 00:49:06,080
So where should we go today?

1325
00:49:06,540 --> 00:49:09,300
There's a new restaurant near the office everyone's talking about.

1326
00:49:09,720 --> 00:49:10,120
Perfect.

1327
00:49:10,300 --> 00:49:10,830
Let's try it.

1328
00:49:11,250 --> 00:49:11,730
Sounds good.

1329
00:49:12,150 --> 00:49:17,840
Well, everyone, we hope today's conversation helped you learn useful English for business meetings and office communication.

1330
00:49:18,200 --> 00:49:21,620
These are practical phrases and expressions you can use at work every day.

1331
00:49:22,060 --> 00:49:26,390
Try practicing them with friends, co-workers, or even by yourself out loud.

1332
00:49:26,490 --> 00:49:30,080
The more you practice, the more confident and natural your English will become.

1333
00:49:30,500 --> 00:49:31,700
Thanks for learning with us today.

1334
00:49:32,160 --> 00:49:35,570
And we'll see you again next time with more Real English Conversations.

1335
00:49:36,050 --> 00:49:36,830
Take care, everyone.

1336
00:49:37,180 --> 00:49:37,800
Bye, everyone.

1337
00:50:14,340 --> 00:50:15,130
Hello, everyone.

1338
00:50:15,490 --> 00:50:18,830
Welcome back to our English Conversation Practice Podcast.

1339
00:50:19,210 --> 00:50:19,670
I'm Ethan.

1340
00:50:20,150 --> 00:50:20,970
And I'm Chloe.

1341
00:50:21,250 --> 00:50:24,220
We're very happy you're spending time learning English with us today.

1342
00:50:24,800 --> 00:50:32,430
On this podcast, we help you improve your English naturally through real conversations and practical workplace situations.

1343
00:50:32,450 --> 00:50:32,970
That's right.

1344
00:50:33,270 --> 00:50:40,030
We use simple and clear English so you can speak more confidently at work, during meetings, and in everyday life.

1345
00:50:40,630 --> 00:50:43,460
And today, we have a very interesting topic for you.

1346
00:50:43,710 --> 00:50:47,530
Today's topic is business meeting conversations in 60 minutes.

1347
00:50:48,190 --> 00:50:51,620
We're going to follow a team through one busy hour at the office.

1348
00:50:52,200 --> 00:51:00,490
During these 60 minutes, they'll prepare for a meeting, discuss problems, share ideas, solve issues, and make important business decisions.

1349
00:51:01,070 --> 00:51:05,490
So you'll learn many useful office expressions and practical meeting vocabulary.

1350
00:51:05,970 --> 00:51:06,740
I'll wait, everyone.

1351
00:51:06,950 --> 00:51:09,040
Let's begin today's conversation practice.

1352
00:51:09,640 --> 00:51:11,200
8 a.m. Monday morning.

1353
00:51:11,520 --> 00:51:12,420
Good morning, Ethan.

1354
00:51:12,480 --> 00:51:13,700
You're here early today.

1355
00:51:13,760 --> 00:51:14,860
Morning, Chloe.

1356
00:51:15,160 --> 00:51:17,640
Yeah, I wanted to prepare before the client meeting starts.

1357
00:51:18,260 --> 00:51:19,050
Smart idea.

1358
00:51:19,390 --> 00:51:21,290
Today's schedule looks very busy.

1359
00:51:21,310 --> 00:51:22,350
Definitely.

1360
00:51:22,530 --> 00:51:25,930
We only have one hour to finalize everything before the client arrives.

1361
00:51:26,430 --> 00:51:26,790
I know.

1362
00:51:26,830 --> 00:51:30,000
I've already received three emails from the manager this morning.

1363
00:51:30,580 --> 00:51:31,080
Same here.

1364
00:51:31,420 --> 00:51:33,400
Did you finish updating the sales presentation?

1365
00:51:33,920 --> 00:51:34,400
Almost.

1366
00:51:34,680 --> 00:51:37,400
I just need to add the latest customer feedback numbers.

1367
00:51:37,990 --> 00:51:38,300
Great.

1368
00:51:38,510 --> 00:51:41,290
The client specifically asked for updated statistics.

1369
00:51:41,590 --> 00:51:42,390
Exactly.

1370
00:51:42,690 --> 00:51:45,930
They want to see how customers responded to the new product launch.

1371
00:51:46,510 --> 00:51:48,570
Honestly, I think the results look pretty good.

1372
00:51:49,030 --> 00:51:49,480
Me too.

1373
00:51:49,980 --> 00:51:52,100
Sales increased faster than we expected.

1374
00:51:52,580 --> 00:51:53,580
That's always good news.

1375
00:51:54,180 --> 00:51:57,280
Unless the finance team starts asking too many questions.

1376
00:51:58,560 --> 00:51:58,820
True.

1377
00:51:59,300 --> 00:52:01,970
They always want detailed explanations for every number.

1378
00:52:02,570 --> 00:52:06,050
Speaking of finance, did Kevin send the final budget report?

1379
00:52:06,530 --> 00:52:08,530
Yes, I received it about 10 minutes ago.

1380
00:52:08,970 --> 00:52:09,470
Perfect.

1381
00:52:09,700 --> 00:52:11,480
That saves us a lot of stress.

1382
00:52:11,760 --> 00:52:12,460
Absolutely.

1383
00:52:12,760 --> 00:52:15,710
Last week, we almost entered a meeting with incomplete information.

1384
00:52:16,230 --> 00:52:17,850
Oh yes, that was a disaster.

1385
00:52:17,910 --> 00:52:20,230
The manager looked so frustrated.

1386
00:52:20,650 --> 00:52:22,910
Especially when the projector stopped working.

1387
00:52:23,440 --> 00:52:24,300
Don't remind me.

1388
00:52:24,780 --> 00:52:26,000
That meeting felt endless.

1389
00:52:26,560 --> 00:52:29,060
Well, hopefully today goes more smoothly.

1390
00:52:29,080 --> 00:52:30,340
I hope so too.

1391
00:52:30,840 --> 00:52:33,190
By the way, have you checked the conference room yet?

1392
00:52:33,710 --> 00:52:34,130
Not yet.

1393
00:52:34,390 --> 00:52:34,590
Why?

1394
00:52:35,150 --> 00:52:37,970
I heard another department was using it earlier this morning.

1395
00:52:38,490 --> 00:52:39,010
Seriously?

1396
00:52:39,460 --> 00:52:41,280
Our meeting starts in less than an hour.

1397
00:52:41,510 --> 00:52:42,010
I know.

1398
00:52:42,310 --> 00:52:43,990
We should make sure the room is ready.

1399
00:52:44,510 --> 00:52:45,030
Good idea.

1400
00:52:45,260 --> 00:52:46,220
Let's go check quickly.

1401
00:52:46,700 --> 00:52:47,040
Wow.

1402
00:52:47,360 --> 00:52:49,040
The room is still full of people.

1403
00:52:49,600 --> 00:52:50,240
Excuse me.

1404
00:52:50,440 --> 00:52:51,560
Are you almost finished here?

1405
00:52:52,140 --> 00:52:52,860
Oh, sorry.

1406
00:52:52,900 --> 00:52:54,240
We're wrapping up right now.

1407
00:52:54,970 --> 00:52:55,260
Thanks.

1408
00:52:55,490 --> 00:52:58,810
We have an important client meeting at 9 a.m. No problem.

1409
00:52:58,990 --> 00:53:00,150
We'll leave in five minutes.

1410
00:53:00,790 --> 00:53:01,470
Thank goodness.

1411
00:53:01,750 --> 00:53:02,550
I was getting nervous.

1412
00:53:03,150 --> 00:53:03,750
Same here.

1413
00:53:04,130 --> 00:53:06,620
We still need to set up the laptops and documents.

1414
00:53:07,240 --> 00:53:08,960
At least the projector's working this time.

1415
00:53:09,540 --> 00:53:11,080
Let's hope it stays that way.

1416
00:53:11,430 --> 00:53:14,540
All right, while they finish up, let's review the meeting agenda.

1417
00:53:15,020 --> 00:53:15,540
Good idea.

1418
00:53:15,600 --> 00:53:18,700
First, we'll welcome the client and introduce the team.

1419
00:53:19,260 --> 00:53:21,490
Then we'll present the quarterly sales report.

1420
00:53:21,970 --> 00:53:25,550
After that, we'll discuss marketing performance and future strategies.

1421
00:53:26,190 --> 00:53:28,520
And finally, we'll answer questions from the client.

1422
00:53:29,060 --> 00:53:30,080
Sounds simple enough.

1423
00:53:30,620 --> 00:53:31,100
Hopefully.

1424
00:53:31,440 --> 00:53:33,780
Clients always ask unexpected questions.

1425
00:53:34,240 --> 00:53:34,800
That's true.

1426
00:53:35,110 --> 00:53:36,530
We should be prepared for anything.

1427
00:53:37,050 --> 00:53:39,310
Especially questions about project delays.

1428
00:53:39,580 --> 00:53:42,320
Yeah, the production team is still behind schedule.

1429
00:53:42,740 --> 00:53:45,000
Do you think the client already knows about the delay?

1430
00:53:45,540 --> 00:53:46,180
Probably.

1431
00:53:46,530 --> 00:53:49,270
They emailed us twice last week asking for updates.

1432
00:53:49,850 --> 00:53:51,730
That could make today's discussion difficult.

1433
00:53:52,290 --> 00:53:55,790
Maybe, but honesty is usually the best approach.

1434
00:53:55,810 --> 00:53:56,220
I agree.

1435
00:53:56,280 --> 00:53:59,120
It's better to explain the problem clearly than hide it.

1436
00:53:59,700 --> 00:54:00,300
Exactly.

1437
00:54:00,620 --> 00:54:02,360
Clients appreciate transparency.

1438
00:54:02,960 --> 00:54:04,640
All right, the room is finally empty.

1439
00:54:04,920 --> 00:54:06,090
Let's start setting everything up.

1440
00:54:06,610 --> 00:54:08,390
I'll arrange the handouts on the table.

1441
00:54:08,650 --> 00:54:08,950
Great.

1442
00:54:09,300 --> 00:54:11,460
I'll connect the presentation slides to the projector.

1443
00:54:11,840 --> 00:54:13,400
Could you also test the speakers?

1444
00:54:14,020 --> 00:54:14,240
Sure.

1445
00:54:14,480 --> 00:54:16,540
We'll need them for the product demonstration video.

1446
00:54:17,060 --> 00:54:17,390
Thanks.

1447
00:54:18,430 --> 00:54:18,510
Hmm.

1448
00:54:18,530 --> 00:54:20,010
The sound seems a little low.

1449
00:54:20,510 --> 00:54:20,770
Really?

1450
00:54:21,350 --> 00:54:21,730
Yeah.

1451
00:54:21,790 --> 00:54:23,230
Let me adjust the settings quickly.

1452
00:54:23,710 --> 00:54:24,270
Good catch.

1453
00:54:24,630 --> 00:54:27,960
Small technical issues can become big problems during meetings.

1454
00:54:28,540 --> 00:54:29,080
Exactly.

1455
00:54:29,640 --> 00:54:30,160
All right.

1456
00:54:30,460 --> 00:54:32,280
I think everything looks ready now.

1457
00:54:32,780 --> 00:54:33,450
Perfect timing.

1458
00:54:33,660 --> 00:54:34,930
The manager just arrived.

1459
00:54:35,450 --> 00:54:36,170
Morning, everyone.

1460
00:54:36,450 --> 00:54:37,750
Are we ready for the client meetings?

1461
00:54:38,030 --> 00:54:39,640
Yes, almost everything is prepared.

1462
00:54:40,100 --> 00:54:40,620
Great work.

1463
00:54:40,880 --> 00:54:45,320
We only have 20 minutes left, so let's review the key discussion points quickly.

1464
00:54:45,820 --> 00:54:46,060
Sure.

1465
00:54:46,610 --> 00:54:49,790
First, we'll highlight the strong sales growth from last quarter.

1466
00:54:50,330 --> 00:54:50,590
Right.

1467
00:54:50,790 --> 00:54:52,890
The numbers improved by nearly 15%.

1468
00:54:52,990 --> 00:54:54,280
Excellent.

1469
00:54:54,530 --> 00:54:55,960
That's a strong selling point.

1470
00:54:56,380 --> 00:54:58,860
We also prepared customer satisfaction reports.

1471
00:54:59,440 --> 00:54:59,700
Good.

1472
00:55:00,020 --> 00:55:03,790
The client always focuses heavily on customer experience.

1473
00:55:04,040 --> 00:55:06,280
Should we mention the shipping delays immediately?

1474
00:55:06,800 --> 00:55:08,300
Yes, but carefully.

1475
00:55:08,620 --> 00:55:11,570
We should explain both the problem and our solution.

1476
00:55:11,610 --> 00:55:12,810
That makes sense.

1477
00:55:13,330 --> 00:55:15,390
We don't want the meeting to sound negative.

1478
00:55:16,010 --> 00:55:16,490
Exactly.

1479
00:55:16,930 --> 00:55:19,260
Confidence is important during business meetings.

1480
00:55:19,840 --> 00:55:20,360
Absolutely.

1481
00:55:20,940 --> 00:55:21,580
One more thing.

1482
00:55:21,900 --> 00:55:26,170
Please remember to keep your answers short and professional during the Q&A session.

1483
00:55:26,770 --> 00:55:27,190
Understood.

1484
00:55:27,730 --> 00:55:30,750
Sometimes long explanations create confusion.

1485
00:55:30,990 --> 00:55:33,210
especially when clients are short on time.

1486
00:55:33,750 --> 00:55:34,170
Correct.

1487
00:55:34,750 --> 00:55:37,150
Excuse me, the clients just arrived downstairs.

1488
00:55:37,730 --> 00:55:38,550
All right, everyone.

1489
00:55:38,820 --> 00:55:40,540
Let's stay calm and professional.

1490
00:55:41,040 --> 00:55:41,940
Good morning, everyone.

1491
00:55:42,260 --> 00:55:43,140
Welcome to our office.

1492
00:55:43,700 --> 00:55:44,160
Thank you.

1493
00:55:44,220 --> 00:55:46,820
It's nice to finally meet everyone in person.

1494
00:55:47,320 --> 00:55:48,670
Please come in and have a seat.

1495
00:55:49,150 --> 00:55:51,690
Would anyone like coffee or tea before we begin?

1496
00:55:52,150 --> 00:55:52,970
Coffee would be great.

1497
00:55:53,150 --> 00:55:53,470
Thank you.

1498
00:55:53,910 --> 00:55:54,330
Of course.

1499
00:55:54,950 --> 00:55:55,370
All right.

1500
00:55:55,570 --> 00:55:56,820
Let's begin today's meeting.

1501
00:55:57,160 --> 00:55:58,500
Thank you all for joining us.

1502
00:55:58,750 --> 00:56:02,910
We're excited to discuss the project's progress and future opportunities together.

1503
00:56:03,490 --> 00:56:05,550
First, let's quickly introduce ourselves.

1504
00:56:06,150 --> 00:56:08,020
I'm Chloe from the marketing department.

1505
00:56:08,620 --> 00:56:10,680
And I'm Ethan from sales operations.

1506
00:56:11,200 --> 00:56:11,700
Wonderful.

1507
00:56:12,040 --> 00:56:14,400
Let's start with the quarterly sales presentation.

1508
00:56:14,760 --> 00:56:15,000
Ethan.

1509
00:56:15,540 --> 00:56:15,920
Thank you.

1510
00:56:16,640 --> 00:56:20,310
Over the past three months, sales performance exceeded our expectations.

1511
00:56:20,890 --> 00:56:21,710
That's great to hear.

1512
00:56:21,750 --> 00:56:26,700
Online sales increased significantly after the launch of our new advertising campaign.

1513
00:56:26,960 --> 00:56:29,040
Which marketing channels performed best?

1514
00:56:29,680 --> 00:56:32,930
Short-form video advertisements generated the highest engagement.

1515
00:56:33,470 --> 00:56:33,990
Interesting.

1516
00:56:34,250 --> 00:56:35,850
That matches current market trends.

1517
00:56:36,410 --> 00:56:36,910
Exactly.

1518
00:56:37,210 --> 00:56:40,970
We also noticed increased customer interaction on social media platforms.

1519
00:56:41,490 --> 00:56:41,970
Excellent.

1520
00:56:42,540 --> 00:56:46,240
However, we did face some shipping delays during peak order periods.

1521
00:56:46,800 --> 00:56:49,500
Yes, we noticed some complaints from customers.

1522
00:56:50,140 --> 00:56:52,020
We completely understand your concern.

1523
00:56:52,520 --> 00:56:56,970
The delays were caused by supplier shortages and increased seasonal demand.

1524
00:56:57,350 --> 00:56:57,930
I see.

1525
00:56:57,970 --> 00:57:00,600
What steps are you taking to improve the situation?

1526
00:57:01,060 --> 00:57:05,280
We're currently expanding warehouse support and improving delivery coordination.

1527
00:57:05,800 --> 00:57:09,020
We also hired temporary staff to reduce processing times.

1528
00:57:09,560 --> 00:57:10,640
That sounds reassuring.

1529
00:57:11,050 --> 00:57:15,030
We expect delivery performance to improve significantly within the next month.

1530
00:57:15,610 --> 00:57:15,970
Excellent.

1531
00:57:16,230 --> 00:57:19,670
Communication and transparency are very important to us.

1532
00:57:19,690 --> 00:57:20,840
We completely agree.

1533
00:57:20,890 --> 00:57:24,240
Now let's discuss future expansion plans.

1534
00:57:24,510 --> 00:57:28,110
We're planning to focus more heavily on international markets next year.

1535
00:57:28,570 --> 00:57:29,290
That's exciting.

1536
00:57:29,790 --> 00:57:31,620
Which regions are you targeting first?

1537
00:57:32,160 --> 00:57:35,880
We're currently researching opportunities in Southeast Asia and Europe.

1538
00:57:36,360 --> 00:57:38,830
Those markets have strong growth potential right now.

1539
00:57:39,330 --> 00:57:39,850
Exactly.

1540
00:57:40,150 --> 00:57:41,930
We believe there's strong demand there.

1541
00:57:42,450 --> 00:57:44,340
Have you considered local partnerships?

1542
00:57:44,920 --> 00:57:48,240
Yes, we're already in discussions with several regional distributors.

1543
00:57:48,760 --> 00:57:49,280
Very good.

1544
00:57:49,600 --> 00:57:51,590
That should help market entry significantly.

1545
00:57:51,610 --> 00:57:52,810
That's our goal.

1546
00:57:53,090 --> 00:57:55,940
Does anyone have additional questions before we wrap up?

1547
00:57:56,480 --> 00:57:59,460
I'd like to ask about the timeline for the next product release.

1548
00:58:00,000 --> 00:58:00,420
Of course.

1549
00:58:00,740 --> 00:58:02,430
We're aiming for early September.

1550
00:58:03,010 --> 00:58:03,290
Great.

1551
00:58:03,570 --> 00:58:05,570
We'll prepare our marketing schedule accordingly.

1552
00:58:06,030 --> 00:58:06,490
Wonderful.

1553
00:58:06,970 --> 00:58:08,640
Thank you everyone for your time today.

1554
00:58:09,100 --> 00:58:11,620
We appreciate the opportunity to work together.

1555
00:58:11,640 --> 00:58:12,060
Thank you.

1556
00:58:12,360 --> 00:58:13,870
This meeting was very productive.

1557
00:58:14,430 --> 00:58:16,110
We look forward to future collaboration.

1558
00:58:16,590 --> 00:58:17,670
Well done, Chloe.

1559
00:58:17,850 --> 00:58:19,660
That meeting went really well.

1560
00:58:19,740 --> 00:58:20,140
Thanks.

1561
00:58:20,560 --> 00:58:22,300
Everyone stayed calm and professional.

1562
00:58:22,940 --> 00:58:25,730
And thankfully, there were no technical disasters this time.

1563
00:58:26,550 --> 00:58:26,850
Yes.

1564
00:58:27,270 --> 00:58:29,510
That alone feels like a huge success.

1565
00:58:30,030 --> 00:58:32,760
I think the clients were happy with our honesty about the delays.

1566
00:58:33,260 --> 00:58:33,800
Definitely.

1567
00:58:34,160 --> 00:58:36,600
Clear communication builds trust.

1568
00:58:36,620 --> 00:58:36,940
Agreed.

1569
00:58:37,420 --> 00:58:40,490
You also handled the difficult questions very confidently.

1570
00:58:40,530 --> 00:58:41,310
Thanks.

1571
00:58:41,830 --> 00:58:43,330
I was nervous at first, honestly.

1572
00:58:43,830 --> 00:58:44,150
Really?

1573
00:58:44,190 --> 00:58:46,390
You looked completely relaxed.

1574
00:58:46,410 --> 00:58:49,660
That's because I practiced my presentation several times this morning.

1575
00:58:49,990 --> 00:58:52,000
Preparation makes a huge difference.

1576
00:58:52,600 --> 00:58:53,120
Absolutely.

1577
00:58:53,660 --> 00:58:57,240
Well, after that stressful hour, I think we deserve coffee.

1578
00:58:57,880 --> 00:58:59,590
I completely agree with that idea.

1579
00:59:00,110 --> 00:59:02,490
Let's grab coffee before the next meeting starts.

1580
00:59:03,090 --> 00:59:04,590
Wait, there's another meeting today?

1581
00:59:05,090 --> 00:59:06,610
Welcome to office life, even.

1582
00:59:06,670 --> 00:59:08,700
Fair enough.

1583
00:59:09,000 --> 00:59:09,380
Let's go.

1584
00:59:09,860 --> 00:59:10,640
All right, everyone.

1585
00:59:10,680 --> 00:59:17,070
We hope you enjoyed today's English conversation practice about business meeting conversations in 60 minutes.

1586
00:59:17,230 --> 00:59:24,520
Today, we practiced useful English for presentations, teamwork, client meetings, problem solving, and office communication.

1587
00:59:25,060 --> 00:59:29,180
These are real expressions you can use in professional situations every day.

1588
00:59:29,240 --> 00:59:33,470
Remember, confidence comes through regular practice and communication.

1589
00:59:33,910 --> 00:59:38,310
Keep practicing your English step by step, and don't be afraid to speak during meetings.

1590
00:59:38,870 --> 00:59:40,940
Thanks so much for learning with us today.

1591
00:59:41,380 --> 00:59:44,540
We'll see you again in the next English conversation practice session.

1592
00:59:45,000 --> 00:59:46,020
Take care, everyone.

1593
00:59:46,170 --> 01:00:08,990
and keep improving your English every single day.
